  quote_by, ph_advantage, ph_notes, kuya_baw_summary, last_updated
) VALUES
  ('IT-001', 'Computer Science', 'Engineering & Tech', FALSE, NULL, 30, 45, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Writing boilerplate code', 'unit test generation', 'code documentation', 'debugging routine errors', 'translating specs into code'], ARRAY['System architecture design', 'security engineering', 'novel algorithm design', 'requirements gathering', 'AI oversight and auditing', 'cross-disciplinary problem framing'], ARRAY['AI Engineer', 'MLOps Engineer', 'AI Governance Officer', 'AI Agent Architect', 'LLM Fine-Tuning Engineer', 'AI Red Team Specialist', 'AI Product Manager'], ARRAY['Python + AI frameworks (PyTorch/HuggingFace/LangChain)', 'RAG and LLM fine-tuning', 'cloud AI platforms (AWS/Azure/GCP)', 'prompt engineering', 'systems design', 'AI ethics'], 'Software developers rank #4 in WEF fastest-growing jobs by absolute numbers through 2030. Junior roles shrink; AI-fluent senior roles expand dramatically.', 'GitHub Copilot generates 46% of all code written by its users; 90% of Fortune 500 companies use it (GitHub 2025)', 'GitHub/Gartner 2025', 'Every young person should become an AI expert. It is an incredible technology that significantly lowers the knowledge barrier of any professional field.', 'Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO', 'UP Diliman (MEng AI; UP Intelligent Systems Center); Mapua (BS AI Engineering — first in PH); DLSU (BS CS + Minor Data Science); Ateneo (ethical AI emphasis)', 'Philippine BPO sector (2M workers) is at high risk of AI disruption; CS graduates who build AI solutions are on the opposite side of that disruption.', 'CS is not dying — it is the most in-demand field because of AI. The job changes from writing all the code yourself to directing AI that writes code and solving the problems AI cannot solve. Learn Python, AI/ML basics, and systems design now.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('IT-004', 'Information Technology', 'Engineering & Tech', FALSE, NULL, 45, 55, 2, 'At Risk', '#EF4444', ARRAY['IT help desk tier-1 support via AI chatbots', 'system monitoring and log analysis', 'routine database queries', 'IT documentation', 'basic network configuration scripts'], ARRAY['Enterprise system integration decisions', 'vendor evaluation', 'cybersecurity incident response', 'business analyst work bridging tech and strategy', 'IT project management', 'change management'], ARRAY['AI Systems Administrator', 'Cybersecurity Analyst', 'BI Developer with AI tools', 'IT AI Integration Specialist', 'Data Governance Analyst', 'No-Code Platform Architect'], ARRAY['Cybersecurity fundamentals (CompTIA Security+)', 'cloud certifications (AWS/Azure/GCP)', 'SQL + Python for data analysis', 'business analysis and requirements gathering', 'ITIL governance frameworks'], 'Routine IT support faces significant pressure. IS professionals bridging business strategy and AI deployment will be highly sought after. Cybersecurity demand is exploding with no signs of slowing.', 'Security management specialists are in WEF top 5 fastest-growing professions globally by 2030 (WEF Future of Jobs 2025)', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025', 'Cybersecurity and data protection roles are growing faster than almost any other profession.', 'World Economic Forum 2025', 'DLSU (BS IT; cybersecurity track); FEU Tech (BS Cybersecurity); Mapua (BS Computer Engineering); TIP Manila (PSM Data Science — first in NCR)', 'Philippine BPO IT roles are among the most exposed to AI automation. Shift toward cybersecurity and business analyst specializations for better long-term security.', 'General IT support jobs face real automation pressure — AI chatbots already handle tier-1 helpdesk. Specialize in cybersecurity, cloud, or business analysis where AI needs humans to supervise it.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-007', 'Computer Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', FALSE, NULL, 20, 30, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Standard HDL module generation', 'routine PCB layout optimization', 'firmware code generation for well-defined tasks', 'simulation and testing automation'], ARRAY['Custom silicon (ASIC/FPGA) architecture design', 'hardware-software co-design for novel AI chips', 'embedded systems for safety-critical applications', 'power delivery and signal integrity engineering'], ARRAY['AI Chip Design Engineer', 'Edge AI Systems Architect', 'Robotics Hardware Engineer', 'Autonomous Vehicle Hardware Engineer', 'Neuromorphic Computing Engineer'], ARRAY['FPGA programming (Xilinx/Intel Vivado)', 'VLSI design basics', 'Embedded AI and TinyML (TensorFlow Lite)', 'IoT systems integration', 'RISC-V architecture', 'PCB design (Altium/KiCad)'], 'Extraordinary demand driven by the AI hardware boom. Every major tech company is designing custom AI chips. CpE graduates who understand both AI software and hardware are among the most globally sought-after engineers.', 'NVIDIA plans to double its workforce to 75000 over the next decade driven by AI chip demand (Fortune 2026)', 'Fortune/NVIDIA 2026', 'Engineers ultimately are the ones that take an invention and advance it in such a way that it is safe, beneficial, and ultimately transformative to society.', 'Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO, April 2026', 'UP Diliman (strong ECE/CpE program); Mapua (BS Computer Engineering); DLSU (BS Computer Engineering); Ateneo (BS CS with hardware tracks)', 'The Philippines has an opportunity to enter the AI chip supply chain as a design hub. CpE graduates with AI hardware knowledge are extremely employable globally.', 'Computer Engineering may be the best-positioned degree in the AI era. NVIDIA, Apple, Google, and Meta are all building custom chips. If you combine hardware and AI knowledge, you are nearly irreplaceable.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-009', 'Electronics & Communications Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'ECE Board Exam', 20, 25, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['RF propagation modeling and simulation', 'antenna pattern optimization via AI', 'circuit simulation and fault detection', 'automated testing and measurement analysis', 'telecom network optimization for 5G cell placement'], ARRAY['Novel RF/antenna system design for new frequency bands (6G)', 'spectrum management and regulatory compliance', 'communication system architecture for defense/aerospace', 'cross-layer protocol design', 'field deployment troubleshooting in complex environments'], ARRAY['5G/6G Network Engineer', 'AI-Powered Signal Processing Engineer', 'Satellite Communications Engineer', 'IoT Systems Engineer', 'Autonomous Vehicle Communications Engineer'], ARRAY['5G/6G standards (3GPP)', 'Software-Defined Radio (SDR)', 'Python for signal processing (NumPy/SciPy)', 'MATLAB/Simulink', 'AI for wireless (beamforming/interference management)', 'IoT protocols (LoRa/MQTT)', 'cybersecurity for comms infrastructure'], 'Strong and growing. BLS projects 9% employment growth 2023-2033 (faster than average). Philippines-specific tailwinds: DICT national broadband program and satellite internet expansion.', 'Employment for electrical and electronics engineers projected to grow 9% from 2023 to 2033 — much faster than average for all occupations (BLS 2025)', 'US Bureau of Labor Statistics 2025', 'The 6G era will require engineers who understand both the physics of wireless propagation and the AI algorithms that will manage spectrum dynamically.', 'IEEE Communications Society 2024', 'UP Diliman (EEEI department; strong ECE tradition); Mapua (accredited ECE program); DLSU (BS Computer Engineering/ECE); UST (ECE program)', 'Philippines needs ECE graduates for DICT broadband programs, PLDT/Globe 5G rollout, and the growing IoT sector across smart cities and agriculture.', 'ECE is a safe and growing career. AI is a tool in your hands — it helps you design better antennas, manage networks faster, and optimize signals automatically. The real work in new frequency bands, defense systems, and satellite comms still needs you.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-008', 'Electrical Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'EE Board Exam', 25, 36, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Power flow analysis and grid optimization calculations', 'routine load calculations and code compliance checks', 'automated high-level synthesis', 'predictive maintenance for electrical equipment', 'energy consumption optimization', 'automated documentation'], ARRAY['Electrical system design for complex facilities', 'power grid stability engineering and fault analysis', 'renewable energy integration and microgrid design', 'safety assessments and hazard analysis (NFPA/NEC)', 'project management on large infrastructure projects', 'field commissioning and troubleshooting'], ARRAY['Renewable Energy Systems Engineer', 'EV Charging Infrastructure Engineer', 'Smart Grid / Energy AI Engineer', 'Battery Systems Engineer', 'AI-Powered Power Systems Analyst', 'Energy Storage Engineer'], ARRAY['Renewable energy systems (solar PV/wind/storage)', 'power electronics and EV technology', 'smart grid technologies and SCADA systems', 'Python for power systems analysis (PyPSA/pandapower)', 'AI for predictive maintenance', 'PLC and industrial automation programming'], 'One of the most future-proof engineering paths. WEF lists Renewable Energy Engineers among top-15 fastest-growing jobs. Philippines has aggressive renewable energy targets creating strong local demand.', 'Renewable Energy Engineers are among WEF''s top 15 fastest-growing jobs globally by 2030 (WEF Future of Jobs 2025)', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025', 'Advances in renewable energy and environmental engineering are expected to increase demand for EE specialists significantly through 2030.', 'WEF/BLS 2025', 'UP Diliman (EEEI department; strong EE research); Mapua (BSME accredited); DLSU (BSEE); Batangas State University (strong EE near industrial zones)', 'Philippines targets 35% renewable energy in power mix by 2030. The energy transition creates massive domestic demand for EEs specialized in solar, wind, and grid integration.', 'EE is one of the safest engineering careers in the AI era. The energy transition to solar, wind, and EVs is creating more EE jobs than AI can eliminate. Add renewable energy and smart grid skills and your career is extremely secure.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-017', 'Mechanical Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'ME Board Exam', 30, 36, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Generative design (AI produces thousands of geometric options from constraints)', 'FEA/CFD simulation setup for standard problems', 'CAD command translation via AI copilots', 'routine technical documentation', 'predictive maintenance modeling', 'standard material selection'], ARRAY['System-level mechanical design judgment', 'manufacturing process engineering (scale-up/tolerancing/DFM)', 'physical testing and prototype development', 'client technical communication', 'safety certification and failure mode analysis', 'novel mechanisms and product innovation'], ARRAY['Robotics Mechanical Engineer', 'AI-Assisted Design Engineer', 'Additive Manufacturing Engineer', 'Digital Twin Engineer', 'Autonomous Vehicle Mechanical Engineer', 'Sustainable Product Design Engineer'], ARRAY['Generative design tools (Fusion 360 Generative/nTopology)', 'FEA/CFD with AI integration (ANSYS/COMSOL)', 'Python for engineering automation', 'additive manufacturing/3D printing', 'Robotics (ROS)', 'digital twin development', 'lifecycle analysis (LCA)'], 'Robust demand driven by robotics, EV manufacturing, and defense/aerospace. Digital twin market projected to grow from $21B to $150B by 2030, creating significant ME demand.', 'Siemens NX AI copilot translates plain-language instructions into CAD commands; early adopters report 40% time savings on design tasks (Siemens/Automate.org 2024)', 'Siemens/Automate.org 2024', 'AI is a design partner, not a replacement for the engineer who must sign off on safety-critical components.', 'ASME 2024 Engineering Leadership Summit', 'UP Diliman (ME; strong research labs); Mapua (BSME accredited); DLSU (BSME); Batangas State University', 'Philippine manufacturing sector (electronics/automotive parts/shipbuilding) creates steady ME demand. Renewable energy and robotics add new growth vectors.', 'ME is transforming, not disappearing. AI now helps you design faster by generating thousands of options automatically. But you still decide which design is safe, manufacturable, and right for the customer. Add robotics and digital twin skills to your toolkit.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-006', 'Civil Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'CE Board Exam', 30, 36, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Structural analysis calculations for standard load cases', 'site survey data processing (AI + drone/LiDAR)', 'quantity takeoffs and cost estimation', 'BIM compliance checking', 'traffic simulation', 'routine inspection report generation from drone footage'], ARRAY['Structural system selection and design philosophy', 'geotechnical investigation interpretation', 'site-specific engineering judgment (typhoon/seismic loads for PH)', 'construction management and contractor coordination', 'community engagement', 'disaster risk reduction and resilience planning'], ARRAY['BIM Specialist', 'Digital Twin Civil Engineer', 'AI-Assisted Structural Engineer', 'Drone Survey/Remote Sensing Engineer', 'Climate Resilience Engineer', 'Smart Infrastructure Engineer'], ARRAY['Revit/AutoCAD Civil 3D (BIM is now industry standard)', 'drone operation and LiDAR data processing', 'GIS for infrastructure planning', 'Python for structural analysis automation', 'climate adaptation and resilience engineering', 'PMP certification'], 'Strong demand in Philippines driven by Build Better More infrastructure program, disaster resilience upgrades, and urbanization. AI shifts CE from calculation to judgment and project leadership.', 'Building construction workers are in WEF top 5 for absolute job growth by 2030 driven by infrastructure and green transition investments (WEF Future of Jobs 2025)', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025', 'The engineer who understands both the algorithm and the ground it stands on will never be replaced by software.', 'ASCE 2025 Infrastructure Report', 'UP Diliman (CE; NICHE Center for disaster risk); Mapua (BS CE accredited); DLSU (BSCE); Batangas State University; MSU-IIT (Mindanao focus)', 'Philippines ranks among most disaster-prone countries globally. Climate resilience engineering is a growing specialty. DPWH infrastructure spending creates consistent CE employment.', 'Civil Engineering is safe and growing in the Philippines. AI takes over the calculations — you do the judgment calls about safety, community impact, and disaster resilience. Learn BIM and drone survey skills and you will be ahead of the curve.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-005', 'Chemical Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'ChE Board Exam', 30, 36, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Process parameter optimization via real-time AI sensor analysis', 'AI-driven formulation development', 'predictive maintenance for plant equipment', 'catalyst/materials discovery screening', 'routine process simulation', 'autonomous lab experiment design'], ARRAY['Process safety and hazard analysis (HAZOP — AI cannot own catastrophic risk decisions)', 'scale-up engineering from lab to plant', 'regulatory and environmental compliance (DENR)', 'novel sustainable process design', 'community and safety accountability on the plant floor'], ARRAY['AI-Augmented Process Engineer', 'Green Chemistry/Sustainable Process Engineer', 'Digital Twin Plant Engineer', 'Materials AI Research Scientist', 'Carbon Capture Process Engineer', 'Battery Materials Engineer'], ARRAY['AI-powered process simulation (Aspen Plus AI features)', 'digital twin development for chemical plants', 'sustainable chemistry and green engineering', 'process safety management (PSM)', 'Python for process data analysis', 'Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) tools'], 'AI cuts research cycles from 18 months to 3 weeks (BASF documented). ChE graduates who master AI-augmented process design will be essential for the green energy transition — battery materials, carbon capture, biofuels.', 'AI has cut BASF chemical research cycles from 18 months to just 3 weeks by mining 150 years of proprietary data (BASF CEO Martin Brudermüller, March 2024)', 'BASF/Martin Brudermüller, March 2024', 'AI is not replacing chemists — it is giving them superpowers.', 'Martin Brudermüller, BASF CEO 2024', 'UP Diliman (BS ChE; Institute of Chemistry); Mapua (BS ChE accredited); DLSU (BS ChE); UST (BS ChE)', 'Philippines has a growing petrochemical, pharmaceutical, and food processing sector. Battery materials (Philippine nickel reserves are 3rd largest globally) create a new high-value specialization for ChE graduates.', 'Chemical Engineering is transforming into AI-augmented research. AI runs simulations and discovers materials faster — you decide what to build, how to scale it safely, and how to meet environmental standards. Add sustainability and battery materials to your focus.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-013', 'Industrial Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'IE Board Exam', 30, 36, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Time-and-motion studies (replaced by AI vision systems)', 'routine work measurement and productivity tracking', 'standard production scheduling optimization', 'quality control inspection (computer vision)', 'basic simulation modeling for standard scenarios'], ARRAY['Systemic problem framing and root cause analysis', 'human factors and ergonomics design', 'organizational change management for AI deployments', 'supply chain strategy and risk management', 'cross-functional team facilitation', 'AI ethics in operations (bias in automated hiring/worker surveillance)'], ARRAY['AI Implementation Engineer', 'Supply Chain AI Analyst', 'Human-Robot Interaction (HRI) Engineer', 'Operations Excellence AI Lead', 'Smart Factory Engineer', 'Workforce Transition/Change Management Specialist'], ARRAY['Simulation software (Arena/FlexSim/AnyLogic)', 'Python for operations research (OR-Tools/PuLP)', 'data analytics (Power BI/Tableau)', 'Lean Six Sigma + AI integration', 'SAP/Oracle supply chain platforms', 'change management certification'], 'IEs are uniquely positioned as AI deployment leaders. Every factory, hospital, logistics company, and BPO deploying automation needs IEs to redesign the workflows. Industry 4.0/5.0 creates enormous demand.', 'The digital twin market is projected to grow from $21 billion in 2025 to $150 billion by 2030 — industrial engineers are central to designing and managing these AI-driven factory systems', 'Digital Twin Market Analysis 2025', 'Industrial engineers are the architects of AI deployment — they decide how humans and machines work together.', 'IISE 2025 Annual Conference', 'UP Diliman (BS IE; Operations Research Center); DLSU (BS IE with strong industry links); Mapua (BS IE); De La Salle Araneta', 'Philippine manufacturing (semiconductor/automotive parts/garments/food processing) and BPO sectors are both undergoing AI-driven transformation. IEs who can lead this change are extremely valuable.', 'IE might be the degree most needed right now. Every company deploying AI needs Industrial Engineers to redesign how humans and machines work together. You are the translator between the AI and the organization — that job is growing, not shrinking.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-012', 'Geodetic Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'GE Board Exam', 25, 30, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Repetitive feature extraction from satellite/aerial imagery', 'automated map generation and cartographic tasks', 'standard topographic survey data processing', 'routine coordinate transformation', 'basic land cover classification', 'GPS data quality control'], ARRAY['Cadastral survey fieldwork and legal boundary adjudication', 'complex terrain interpretation requiring local knowledge', 'disaster risk mapping', 'land use planning policy and stakeholder engagement', 'ground-truthing and validation of AI-generated outputs'], ARRAY['GeoAI Specialist', 'Remote Sensing Data Scientist', 'Drone Survey Engineer/UAS Operator', 'Digital Twin Geospatial Engineer', 'Climate Change Mapping Specialist', 'Smart City GIS Analyst', 'Precision Agriculture GIS Specialist'], ARRAY['ArcGIS Pro/QGIS + Python scripting', 'Google Earth Engine (cloud-scale geospatial analysis)', 'drone operation and photogrammetry (Pix4D/DJI Terra)', 'LiDAR data processing', 'Python for GeoAI (GeoPandas/Rasterio)', '3D city modeling'], 'Geospatial data demand is exploding. Precision agriculture, disaster risk management, urban planning, and climate monitoring all need GEs with AI skills. The field transitions from map-making to insight generation.', 'AI is pushing the geospatial sector away from producing maps and towards generating insights automatically and continuously (Esri/ArcGIS 2024)', 'Esri ArcNews 2024', 'GeoAI represents the convergence of spatial intelligence and machine learning — geodetic engineers who master both will shape how we understand our physical world.', 'Esri/National Geographic 2024', 'UP Diliman (BS Geodetic Engineering; NAMRIA partnership); Mindanao State University; CLSU', 'Philippines has active engagement with NAMRIA and PHIVOLCS. GEs with AI/drone skills are critical for disaster preparedness mapping and CLUP updates.', 'Geodetic Engineering is evolving from survey fieldwork to AI-powered insight generation. The satellite data, the LiDAR, the drones — all those produce massive datasets that GEs interpret. Add GIS scripting and drone photogrammetry and your career scope triples.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-020', 'Metallurgical Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'MetE Board Exam', 35, 40, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Materials property prediction via ML', 'routine alloy composition optimization', 'failure mode analysis for standard materials', 'automated QC via computer vision for defects', 'literature mining', 'standard corrosion modeling'], ARRAY['Novel alloy development for extreme applications (aerospace/defense)', 'process metallurgy on the production floor', 'materials selection for safety-critical components', 'forensic failure analysis requiring physical judgment', 'sustainable metallurgy and recycling', 'critical mineral supply chain management'], ARRAY['Battery Materials Engineer', 'Critical Minerals Supply Chain Engineer', 'AI-Augmented Materials Scientist', 'Additive Manufacturing Materials Engineer (metal 3D printing)', 'Hydrogen Economy Materials Engineer', 'Circular Economy Recycling Process Engineer'], ARRAY['Computational materials science (CALPHAD/VASP/Python)', 'ML for materials discovery (materials informatics)', 'battery technology and electrochemistry fundamentals', 'additive manufacturing for metals (SLS/DMLS)', 'critical mineral processing (Li/Ni/Co for EVs)', 'AI materials databases (Materials Project/AFLOW)'], 'EV battery and renewable energy transition creates enormous demand. Philippines-specific: country has world''s 3rd largest nickel reserves — MetE graduates with battery chemistry knowledge are strategically positioned.', 'Philippines holds the world''s 3rd largest nickel reserves — metallurgical engineers with battery chemistry knowledge are strategically positioned for the EV materials supply chain (MGB/USGS 2025)', 'Mines and Geosciences Bureau/USGS 2025', 'The energy transition is a metallurgical engineering problem as much as it is an electrical engineering problem.', 'Rocky Mountain Institute 2024', 'UP Diliman (BS Metallurgical Engineering; IESM institute); Mapua (MetE program); DLSU; PLM', 'Philippine nickel, copper, and chromite mining sector creates consistent employment. The EV battery revolution elevates this — nickel from Palawan and Surigao is now a strategic global commodity.', 'Metallurgical Engineering is more valuable than ever because of the EV revolution. Every electric car needs battery materials — nickel, cobalt, lithium — that MetE graduates know how to process. The Philippines'' mineral wealth makes this especially relevant for you.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-024', 'Sanitary Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'SE Board Exam', 30, 40, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Real-time water quality monitoring and alert systems', 'AI-driven water treatment plant optimization', 'automated wastewater treatment process control', 'pollution source tracking via ML', 'routine environmental compliance report generation', 'water demand forecasting'], ARRAY['Water system master planning and infrastructure design', 'community health impact assessment', 'regulatory negotiation and permitting', 'emergency response and crisis management for water/sanitation systems', 'policy advocacy for water security', 'community engagement for sanitation programs in developing contexts'], ARRAY['AI Water Treatment Systems Engineer', 'Smart Water Network Manager', 'Climate-Resilient WASH Engineer', 'Environmental Data Scientist', 'Water Security Analyst', 'One Health Systems Engineer'], ARRAY['IoT sensor networks for environmental monitoring', 'AI/ML for water quality prediction', 'GIS for watershed management', 'Python for environmental data analysis', 'climate change adaptation for water systems', 'SCADA systems for water utilities'], 'Strong demand in developing countries including the Philippines. UNICEF estimates 2.2 billion people lack safe water. Climate change creates new urgency for sanitary engineers.', 'AI is rapidly emerging as a driving force for water treatment technology — demonstrating potential in data analysis, process prediction, and resource allocation (Frontiers of Environmental Science and Engineering 2025)', 'Frontiers of Environmental Science and Engineering 2025', 'Clean water is a human right that no algorithm can deliver on its own — it requires engineers who understand both the infrastructure and the community.', 'UNICEF Water Security Report 2024', 'UP Diliman (Institute of Civil Engineering/Environmental Engineering); Mapua (SanE); DLSU; UST', 'Philippines ranked 81st globally in water access (WHO/UNICEF 2023). MWSS, LWUA, and LGU water districts consistently hire SanE graduates. Climate change and population growth make water security a national priority.', 'Sanitary Engineering is extremely secure — clean water is a fundamental human need that AI cannot deliver without you. AI helps you monitor water quality in real time and optimize treatment plants, but the infrastructure design, community work, and regulatory compliance are yours.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-001', 'Agricultural Engineering', 'Engineering & Tech', TRUE, 'AgriE Board Exam', 35, 45, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Crop yield prediction using satellite imagery and ML', 'automated irrigation scheduling', 'drone-based crop health monitoring', 'soil analysis and fertilizer recommendation algorithms', 'autonomous tractor route optimization', 'routine IoT sensor data collection'], ARRAY['Agricultural system design for specific local conditions (typhoon resilience in PH)', 'community-level agricultural development programs', 'novel crop variety adaptation engineering', 'rural infrastructure design (post-harvest/irrigation networks)', 'food security policy', 'integration of traditional farming knowledge with technology'], ARRAY['Precision Agriculture Engineer/AgTech Specialist', 'Drone Agronomy Technician', 'Agricultural AI Data Analyst', 'Smart Irrigation Systems Engineer', 'Climate-Smart Agriculture Engineer', 'Food Systems Engineer', 'Vertical Farming/CEA Engineer'], ARRAY['Precision agriculture platforms (John Deere Operations Center/Trimble)', 'drone operation for agricultural applications', 'IoT for agriculture (soil sensors/weather stations)', 'GIS and remote sensing for crop monitoring', 'Python for agricultural data analysis', 'post-harvest technology and cold chain management'], 'WEF 2025 projects farmworkers and agricultural roles as the single largest job growth category globally — 34 million new jobs added by 2030. Philippine food security agenda and climate-smart agriculture push under DA create strong domestic demand.', 'GeoAI empowers farmers and policymakers to tackle drought, pest outbreaks, and soil degradation through precision agriculture and predictive modeling (ScienceDirect/Esri 2025)', 'ScienceDirect/Esri 2025', 'Precision agriculture AI tools could increase crop yields 15-20% while reducing water use by 30% — creating high demand for agricultural professionals who can operate these systems.', 'McKinsey Global Institute 2023', 'UPLB (University of the Philippines Los Baños — premier agri university in PH); VSU (Visayas State University); BSU Benguet; CLSU; Batangas State University', 'Philippines is highly vulnerable to climate change with agriculture as the most affected sector. DA SAAD program and the emerging AgTech startup scene create new pathways for tech-integrated agriculturists.', 'Agricultural Engineering is one of the most important careers for the Philippines future. AI tools let you monitor crops by drone, automate irrigation, and predict yields from satellite data — but you design the systems, train the farmers, and adapt the technology to Philippine conditions.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-008', 'Medicine', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Physician Licensure Exam (PLE)', 15, 25, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Medical imaging interpretation (1039 FDA-authorized AI radiology devices as of Dec 2025)', 'AI-assisted diagnostics for dermatology/ophthalmology/pathology', 'clinical documentation via AI scribes', 'initial patient triage and risk stratification', 'literature search and differential diagnosis generation'], ARRAY['Physical examination requiring touch and observation', 'surgical procedures (robot-assisted surgery still requires surgeon control)', 'doctor-patient relationship and empathy', 'complex ethical decisions (end-of-life care)', 'accountability and legal responsibility for clinical decisions'], ARRAY['Clinical AI Integrationist/Physician Informaticist', 'AI-Assisted Diagnostics Specialist', 'Digital Health Medical Director', 'Telehealth Physician', 'Clinical AI Trainer'], ARRAY['AI literacy (understanding diagnostic AI tools and their limitations)', 'health informatics and EHR optimization', 'telehealth consultation skills', 'data interpretation for AI-generated risk scores', 'critical appraisal of AI-assisted diagnoses (avoiding automation bias)'], 'Physicians who adopt AI tools will be significantly more productive and competitive. WEF projects 30% growth in demand for health professionals despite AI adoption.', 'FDA had authorized 1039 AI-enabled radiology devices by December 2025 — over 80% of all approved AI medical devices (The Imaging Wire/FDA 2025)', 'The Imaging Wire/FDA December 2025', 'Doctors who don''t use AI will be replaced by doctors who do.', 'Fortune November 2025', 'UP Manila (College of Medicine — PH top medical school); UST Faculty of Medicine and Surgery; Ateneo School of Medicine and Public Health (ASMPH); De La Salle Medical and Health Sciences Institute; FEU-NRMF', 'Philippines has a doctor-to-population ratio of approximately 1:33000 (far below WHO recommended 1:1000). AI tools that extend the reach of Filipino physicians are urgently needed.', 'Medicine is one of the safest careers in the AI era. AI helps you read X-rays faster and catch diagnoses you might miss — but you are still the one who examines the patient, explains the diagnosis, makes the ethical call, and signs the prescription. AI makes you a better doctor, not a jobless one.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('HLT-005', 'Nursing', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Nurse Licensure Exam (NLE)', 12, 15, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['Nursing documentation and shift notes via AI scribes', 'medication scheduling and reminders', 'patient monitoring alerts via AI wearables', 'appointment scheduling and triage scoring', 'routine patient education content delivery'], ARRAY['Hands-on bedside care/wound care/patient mobilization', 'emotional support and therapeutic communication', 'clinical judgment in rapidly changing patient conditions', 'administering medications and monitoring real-time patient responses', 'advocating for patients in multidisciplinary teams', 'end-of-life nursing care'], ARRAY['Nurse Informaticist/Clinical Informatics Specialist', 'Telehealth Nurse/Remote Patient Monitoring Nurse', 'AI Care Coordinator', 'Healthcare AI Trainer (clinical nursing)', 'Community Health Nurse'], ARRAY['Digital literacy with EHR systems and AI monitoring tools', 'telehealth platform proficiency', 'data interpretation (reading AI-generated patient risk scores)', 'leadership and care coordination skills', 'critical thinking in AI-assisted clinical environments'], 'Nursing remains one of the most AI-resistant healthcare professions. WEF projects a shortfall of 10 million healthcare workers by 2030. Hospitals invest in AI because they cannot hire enough nurses — not to replace them.', 'Nursing has only a 12% automation risk — core bedside care tasks have the lowest automation rate of any health profession (Anthropic Labor Market Report 2026)', 'Anthropic Labor Market Report/aichanging.work 2026', 'Hospitals are not investing in AI to replace nurses. They are investing in AI because they cannot hire enough nurses.', 'HealthLeaders Media 2025', 'UST (College of Nursing — consistently top board passers); UP Manila (College of Nursing); Cebu Normal University; San Pedro College; San Juan de Dios College', 'Philippines is the world''s largest exporter of nurses. Global demand is growing — the US, UK, Saudi Arabia, and Australia all have critical nursing shortages. AI makes Filipino nurses more productive but cannot replace bedside care.', 'Nursing is one of the safest careers you can choose. AI takes over the paperwork and monitoring alerts so you can focus on patients. The global demand for nurses is only growing — the US and EU have critical shortages they cannot fill. Your skills will be needed everywhere.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('HLT-003', 'Medical Technology', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Medical Technology Board Exam', 25, 40, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Automated analyzers for CBC/chemistry panels/urinalysis (already widely deployed)', 'AI-assisted reading of blood smears/Pap smears/histopathology slides (51 FDA-authorized pathology AI devices)', 'robotic sample handling', 'automated result verification', 'inventory management and QC flagging'], ARRAY['Troubleshooting instrument errors and unusual results', 'interpreting clinically ambiguous or critical values in patient context', 'specimen rejection decisions', 'managing rare or complex sample types', 'communicating critical results to physicians', 'quality assurance program design'], ARRAY['Laboratory Informatics Specialist', 'AI-Augmented Pathology Technologist', 'Clinical Data Analyst (lab data + AI)', 'Point-of-Care Testing (POCT) Coordinator', 'Lab Automation Systems Manager'], ARRAY['Laboratory information systems (LIS) proficiency', 'understanding automated analyzer AI flags and limitations', 'basic bioinformatics and data analytics', 'quality management systems', 'molecular diagnostics (PCR/next-gen sequencing)'], 'Routine bench work will be heavily automated, but MedTechs who can operate, validate, and troubleshoot AI-integrated lab systems will be indispensable. A global shortage of skilled lab technicians protects employment.', 'The lab automation market is projected to grow from $6.36 billion (2025) to $9.01 billion by 2030 at 7.2% CAGR (MarketsandMarkets 2025)', 'MarketsandMarkets 2025', 'By automating routine tasks such as document review, case triage, and data summarization, AI frees up staff to focus on higher-value work.', 'Mayo Clinic Laboratories 2025', 'UP Manila (College of Allied Medical Professions); UST (Medical Technology — consistently top board passers); SWU Cebu; Far Eastern University; Emilio Aguinaldo College', 'Philippine medical laboratories are adopting automated analyzers rapidly — COVID-19 accelerated this significantly. MedTechs who can manage and troubleshoot these systems are in high demand.', 'Medical Technology is transforming, not disappearing. AI runs the routine tests automatically — you verify the unusual results, troubleshoot the instrument errors, and make judgment calls on complex specimens. Add LIS and molecular diagnostics skills.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('HLT-009', 'Physical Therapy', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Physical Therapy Board Exam', 3, 6, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['Scheduling and billing', 'motion capture and movement analysis via AI apps', 'remote exercise monitoring', 'documentation and clinical note generation', 'outcome tracking dashboards'], ARRAY['Manual therapy (joint mobilization/soft tissue work/dry needling — requires trained hands)', 'real-time clinical reasoning during treatment', 'therapeutic exercise progression based on subjective patient response', 'patient motivation and behavioral change coaching', 'complex neurological and pediatric rehabilitation'], ARRAY['Digital Rehabilitation Specialist', 'Rehabilitation Technology Analyst', 'Virtual PT Coach (AI + human hybrid)', 'Sports Performance AI Analyst', 'Telehealth Physical Therapist'], ARRAY['AI-powered motion analysis tools (Kaia Health/Hinge Health platforms)', 'telehealth consultation and remote monitoring', 'understanding wearable sensor data', 'motivational interviewing for digital health engagement', 'specialization in sports rehab/pediatrics/neuro'], 'PT is one of the most automation-resistant healthcare careers. BLS projects 14% employment growth through 2033. AI enhances the profession by allowing PTs to spend 30% more time on direct patient care.', 'Physical therapists rank among the 6 professions LEAST likely to be replaced by robots out of 702 occupations — only 0.4% automation probability (WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/Oxford Frey-Osborne methodology)', 'WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/Oxford Frey-Osborne 2025', 'Physical therapy requires the integration of scientific knowledge, clinical reasoning, and human connection that cannot be replicated by any algorithm.', 'American Physical Therapy Association (APTA) 2025', 'UP Manila (College of Allied Medical Professions); UST (PT program); Our Lady of Fatima University; CEU (Centro Escolar University); Cebu Doctors University', 'Philippines has one of Southeast Asia''s most respected PT training programs with high global mobility — PTs are in demand in the US, Canada, Australia, and UAE.', 'Physical Therapy is one of the safest careers you can choose. The hands-on healing you provide — the joint mobilizations, the rehabilitation exercises, the therapeutic relationship — cannot be replicated by any machine. AI helps you track progress and reduce paperwork. Your career is secure.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('HLT-007', 'Occupational Therapy', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Occupational Therapy Board Exam', 0, 1, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['Administrative workflow (scheduling/billing/prior authorization)', 'progress note generation and report writing', 'data analytics for functional improvement trends', 'recommending assistive device options based on patient profiles'], ARRAY['ADL (Activities of Daily Living) training requiring physical guidance and observation', 'cognitive rehabilitation sessions requiring human judgment', 'home assessment visits', 'pediatric sensory integration therapy', 'mental health OT', 'building therapeutic rapport with patients with disabilities'], ARRAY['Assistive Technology Specialist (AI-powered adaptive devices)', 'Digital OT/Telehealth Occupational Therapist', 'VR Rehabilitation Therapist', 'Ergonomics AI Analyst', 'Occupational Health Informatics Consultant'], ARRAY['Assistive technology (eye-tracking devices/brain-computer interfaces/smart home tech)', 'VR/AR rehabilitation tools', 'telehealth OT platforms', 'collaboration with AI-driven adaptive device teams', 'specialization in pediatrics/geriatrics/mental health'], 'Extremely safe career. Demand driven by aging populations, mental health awareness, and pediatric developmental needs — all requiring irreplaceable human connection.', 'Occupational therapy was scored as the 6th-to-last profession of 702 to be replaced by robots — 0.4% automation probability (WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/Frey and Osborne methodology 2025)', 'WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/Frey and Osborne 2025', 'AI does not replace judgment — it reveals it. When technology takes care of the redundant, we are left with what only humans can do: connect, explain, comfort, and decide.', 'AOTA (American Occupational Therapy Association) 2025', 'UP Manila (College of Allied Medical Professions); Our Lady of Fatima University; UST; Cebu Doctors University; Manila Central University', 'OT is an emerging field in the Philippines with growing awareness of pediatric development disorders, aging population needs, and workplace ergonomics. High demand, low supply.', 'Occupational Therapy has one of the lowest AI automation risks of any profession — 0.4% according to Oxford research. You work with people recovering function and learning to live with disabilities. No AI can sit with a patient and guide them through those deeply human moments.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('HLT-001', 'Dentistry', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Dentist Licensure Exam', 5, 15, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['Dental radiograph analysis — AI detects caries/periodontal disease/oral cancer (often exceeding human accuracy)', 'treatment planning recommendations', 'clinical note transcription', 'appointment scheduling and billing', 'CAD/CAM digital dental lab work', 'patient risk scoring for preventive care'], ARRAY['All surgical and procedural dentistry (extractions/implants/restorations/root canals)', 'patient consultation and treatment consent', 'interpretation of AI diagnoses in clinical context', 'handling patient anxiety and dental fear', 'prosthetics fitting requiring tactile and aesthetic judgment', 'pediatric and special needs dental care'], ARRAY['AI Dental Diagnostics Specialist (operating Overjet/Pearl AI platforms)', 'Digital Dental Workflow Coordinator', 'Dental Implant/Robotics Surgeon', 'Tele-Dentistry Practitioner', 'Oral Health Informatics Specialist'], ARRAY['AI diagnostic software (Overjet/Pearl/Denti.AI)', 'digital dentistry (CAD/CAM/intraoral scanning/CBCT interpretation)', 'tele-dentistry platforms', 'implant and surgical technology integration', 'oral cancer detection AI oversight'], 'The dental practice shifts to augmented dentistry — AI handles analysis, dentist handles patient and procedure. AI dental market growing at 26.5% CAGR, projected to reach $2.7 billion by 2030.', 'General dentists are scored at 0.0% automation probability — the lowest risk rating possible (WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/Oxford methodology 2025); 35% of dental practices already use AI as of 2025', 'WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/GoTu 2025', 'AI analyzing radiographs detects caries, periodontal disease, and oral cancer with accuracy often exceeding human practitioners — but the dentist still drills, fills, and builds the patient relationship.', 'PubMed/PMC 2025', 'UP Manila (College of Dentistry — consistently ranked #1 in board exams); UST (College of Dentistry); DLSU Health Sciences; Centro Escolar University; University of the East Manila', 'Philippines has a dentist-to-population ratio of approximately 1:35000 (far below WHO recommendation of 1:5000). Dental health is severely underserved, especially outside Metro Manila. AI increases each dentist''s productivity significantly.', 'Dentistry is one of the most AI-proof careers available. The procedures you perform — fillings, extractions, root canals, implants — require your hands, your training, and your judgment. AI helps you catch what you might miss on an X-ray. Your career is safe and the demand in the Philippines is enormous.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('HLT-008', 'Pharmacy', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Pharmacist Licensure Exam', 28, 44, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Drug dispensing robots (automated pill counting/packaging/labeling — already deployed in hospitals)', 'drug interaction and contraindication checking via AI', 'inventory management and auto-reordering', 'prior authorization processing', 'routine medication refill management'], ARRAY['Patient medication counseling (explaining side effects and adherence coaching)', 'complex polypharmacy management for elderly/chronic disease patients', 'clinical pharmacy consultations in hospitals', 'compounding (custom medication preparation)', 'pharmacovigilance and adverse event monitoring'], ARRAY['Clinical Pharmacist (expanded role in patient care teams)', 'Pharmacogenomics Specialist', 'AI Pharmacy Technologist', 'Drug Information Specialist', 'Pharmaceutical Data Scientist', 'Telepharmacy Practitioner'], ARRAY['Pharmacogenomics and precision medicine', 'clinical pharmacy practice (MTM — Medication Therapy Management)', 'understanding AI drug discovery tools (AlphaFold/generative chemistry)', 'telepharmacy technology', 'data analytics and pharmacovigilance systems'], 'Dispensing tasks automate, but clinical pharmacy expands significantly. The pharmacist role evolves from dispenser to clinical consultant. Healthcare AI job postings mentioning pharmacy skills grew 42% YoY in 2025.', 'AI drug discovery is cutting pharma R&D timelines by up to 50%, but no AI-discovered drug has yet received FDA approval as of December 2025 — pharmacists remain essential (DataM Intelligence/FDA 2025)', 'DataM Intelligence/FDA 2025', 'AI and robots will not replace pharmacists by 2030, but they will replace the parts of the job that never needed a clinician.', 'PharmacyFreak.com 2025', 'UP Manila (College of Pharmacy); UST (College of Pharmacy); Cebu Doctors University; Adamson University; Our Lady of Fatima University', 'Philippines has a growing pharmaceutical manufacturing sector. Clinical pharmacy is underutilized — most Filipino pharmacists still work primarily in retail dispensing, which is most exposed to automation.', 'Pharmacy is transforming — the robot can count the pills, but it cannot counsel your patient on how to take five medications without side effects or flag the dangerous interaction the doctor missed. Shift your focus toward clinical pharmacy and pharmacogenomics for a strong future.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('HLT-006', 'Nutrition and Dietetics', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Nutritionist-Dietitian Board Exam', 30, 40, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Automated meal planning and dietary analysis (AI apps already do this for consumers)', 'routine nutritional assessments and screening', 'calorie/macro tracking apps replacing basic check-ins', 'automated patient education content', 'NutriGenomics data interpretation'], ARRAY['Complex clinical nutrition in ICU/oncology/renal disease/eating disorders', 'motivational interviewing and long-term behavior change coaching', 'navigating cultural food preferences and socioeconomic barriers (critical in Philippines)', 'multidisciplinary team integration for medically complex patients', 'community nutrition programs and public health policy work'], ARRAY['AI Dietitian/Digital Nutrition Coach', 'Nutrigenomics Consultant', 'Digital Health Coach (AI-enabled remote nutrition counseling)', 'Food Technology-Nutrition Integration Specialist', 'Corporate Wellness AI Program Manager'], ARRAY['AI nutrition assessment tools (Nutritics/Cronometer AI)', 'telehealth nutrition counseling platforms', 'nutrigenomics and precision nutrition', 'digital literacy and basic AI fluency (interpreting AI dietary outputs)', 'community and public health nutrition'], 'Routine nutrition advice is increasingly commoditized by AI apps, but licensed clinical dietitians remain essential for medically complex patients and public health. New hybrid AI Dietitian roles are emerging.', 'By 2025, 40% of nutrition-related tasks are projected to involve some degree of automation; WEF projects 20% rise in demand for human decision-making roles in food/nutrition fields (Research.com/WEF 2026)', 'Research.com/WEF 2026', 'AI can suggest a meal plan, but it cannot sit with a malnourished child''s mother and understand why she cannot follow it.', 'UN Food and Agriculture Organization/Nutrition International 2024', 'UP Diliman (Institute of Human Nutrition and Food); UST (Nutrition and Dietetics); DLSU (Nutrition and Dietetics); Silliman University; Xavier University Cagayan de Oro', 'Philippines faces a dual burden of malnutrition — obesity and undernutrition coexist. Community nutrition roles in DSWD, DOH, and NGOs are resistant to automation. The Philippine nutrition-dietetics profession is undersupplied relative to population.', 'Your career as a nutritionist is safe in the areas that matter most — clinical nutrition for sick patients, community health programs, and the complex behavioral work of helping people change their eating habits. AI apps can give general advice but they cannot replace your clinical judgment.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-014', 'Veterinary Medicine', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Veterinarian Licensure Exam', 5, 10, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['AI radiograph analysis for animals', 'consultation transcription and medical record summarization', 'predictive analytics for disease risk in animal populations', 'triage chatbots for pet owner queries', 'practice management (scheduling/billing/inventory)'], ARRAY['Physical examination and hands-on diagnostics', 'surgery and anesthesia', 'emergency critical care', 'euthanasia and end-of-life conversations with pet owners (deeply human)', 'complex differential diagnosis with behavioral and environmental context', 'large animal/food animal veterinary work in the field'], ARRAY['Veterinary Informaticist', 'Veterinary Telehealth Practitioner', 'Animal AI Diagnostics Technician', 'One Health Data Scientist', 'Livestock/Precision Agriculture Health Specialist'], ARRAY['Veterinary AI diagnostic software (Signify AI for radiology)', 'telehealth/telemedicine for companion animals', 'One Health approach (connecting animal/human/environmental health)', 'food safety and public health veterinary practice', 'data interpretation for herd health AI analytics'], 'Strong growth career — nearly 55000 additional veterinarians needed by 2030 (US alone), with projected shortage of 24000 even accounting for new graduates. AI augments the practice but cannot address the workforce shortage.', 'Veterinarians are scored at 7% automation probability — one of the lowest of any licensed profession (WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/Oxford methodology 2025); 20% projected job growth 2020-2030 (BLS)', 'WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com/BLS 2025', 'AI does not replace judgment — it reveals it. When technology takes care of the redundant, we are left with what only humans can do: connect, explain, comfort, and decide.', 'Covetrus.com 2025', 'UP Los Baños (College of Veterinary Medicine — premier PH institution); Pampanga Agriculture College; Bulacan Agricultural State College; Mindanao 