  ('ENG-011', 'Food Technology', 'Health & Medical', TRUE, 'Food Technologist Licensure Exam', 35, 40, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Automated visual inspection and defect detection on production lines (AI vision systems)', 'contamination and foreign object detection replacing manual QC', 'sorting/grading/packaging tasks via robotic systems', 'supply chain traceability and compliance monitoring', 'predictive shelf-life modeling', 'recipe optimization using AI'], ARRAY['New product development (sensory evaluation/consumer insight integration)', 'regulatory affairs and food safety certification (requires human accountability)', 'supplier relationship management', 'crisis management (food recalls/safety incidents)', 'sensory science (taste/texture/aroma evaluation — human senses)', 'R&D for functional foods and novel food technologies'], ARRAY['AI Food Quality Analyst', 'Food Data Scientist (AI + food production data)', 'Precision Fermentation/Cultivated Meat Technology Specialist', 'Food Regulatory AI Compliance Officer', 'Smart Packaging and Traceability Specialist', 'Consumer Insights Data Analyst'], ARRAY['AI-powered food safety and QC systems', 'data analytics and food production databases', 'regulatory affairs for novel foods', 'sustainability and lifecycle assessment tools', 'sensory science', 'HACCP and food safety management systems'], 'Food Technology evolves toward data-driven food science. The AI in Food Safety and Quality Control market is projected from $2.7B (2024) to $13.7B by 2030 at 30.9% CAGR.', 'The AI in Food Safety and Quality Control Market is projected to grow from $2.7 billion (2024) to $13.7 billion by 2030 at a CAGR of 30.9% (BCC Research 2025)', 'BCC Research 2025', 'Over 60% of AI adoption in food manufacturing in 2025 focuses on quality inspection and contamination detection — replacing visual inspection roles, not food scientists.', 'BCC Research/Frontiers in Sustainable Food Systems 2025', 'UPLB (Institute of Food Science and Technology — #1 in PH); UST (Food Technology); DLSU; FEU; De La Salle Araneta University', 'Philippine food manufacturing industry (processed foods/beverages/snacks) is a major employer. Export markets (US/Japan/EU) require stringent food safety compliance. New product development for Filipino tastes remains deeply human.', 'Food Technology is changing but not disappearing. AI will automate the inspection and sorting on the factory floor, but who designs the new snack that captures Filipino taste preferences? Who navigates the FDA/BFAD approval process? Who handles the food recall crisis? That is still you.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('BUS-001', 'Accountancy', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'CPA Board Exam (CPALE)', 65, 85, 2, 'At Risk', '#EF4444', ARRAY['Data entry and bookkeeping (Quickbooks AI/Xero/FreshBooks)', 'bank reconciliation and transaction categorization', 'basic tax preparation', 'audit sampling and initial risk flagging', 'invoice processing and accounts payable/receivable', 'financial statement generation', 'work traditionally done by first- and second-year staff accountants at Big 4 firms'], ARRAY['Complex tax strategy and advisory (multi-entity/cross-border/estate planning)', 'audit judgment — signing off on opinions', 'ethics decisions and regulatory interpretation', 'client relationship management and financial counseling', 'forensic accounting (fraud investigations)', 'restructuring and M&A advisory', 'board-level financial strategy'], ARRAY['AI Accounting Analyst', 'AI-Powered Auditor', 'Financial Systems Architect', 'AI Risk and Controls Specialist', 'Prompt Engineer for Tax', 'Data Governance Officer', 'AI Compliance Analyst', 'Advisory/CFO-as-a-Service roles'], ARRAY['AI tool proficiency (Copilot for Finance/Intuit Assist/Xero AI/SAP AI)', 'data analytics (Excel/Power BI/Python for financial modeling)', 'prompt engineering for financial queries', 'critical evaluation of AI-generated outputs', 'forensic accounting', 'specialization in complex niches (transfer pricing/ESG reporting)'], 'The CPA credential remains highly valuable but entry-level grunt work is being automated at Big 4 firms. New graduates must demonstrate advisory, analytical, and AI-oversight skills from day one. Accounting jobs requiring AI skills jumped 67% YoY (Accounting Today 2026).', 'Big Four cut graduate hiring — KPMG trimmed 2023 graduate intake by 29%, Deloitte by 18%, EY by 11%, PwC by 6%, citing automation of entry-level tasks (Scottish Financial News/NCS Corp 2025)', 'Scottish Financial News/NCS Corp 2025', 'The Big Four have collectively scaled back graduate hiring as automation tools increasingly carry out basic research, draft content, summarize documents, and check compliance — work traditionally done by new graduates.', 'Scottish Financial News 2025', 'UP Diliman (BS Accountancy — consistently produces top board passers); DLSU (consistently #1 or #2 in CPALE); Ateneo SOB; UST; PLM', 'Philippine accounting profession is large and well-respected globally. Filipino CPAs are in demand in the US, Middle East, and Singapore. However, entry-level BPO accounting roles are at high risk. CPALE holders who add AI skills and advisory capabilities are well-positioned.', 'Accountancy is honest: entry-level accounting tasks are being automated fast. The bookkeeping, the data entry, the routine audit sampling — AI does it better. But the licensed CPA who advises on complex tax strategy, forensic accounting, and financial decisions is more valuable than ever. You need to aim for that advisory role from day one.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-006', 'Business Administration', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 35, 65, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Scheduling and calendar management', 'basic market research compilation', 'routine report generation and data dashboards', 'customer service chatbots for Tier 1 queries', 'inventory management and supply chain optimization', 'payroll processing', 'basic financial analysis', 'content drafting (proposals/memos/standard correspondence)'], ARRAY['Strategic planning and complex decision-making', 'stakeholder negotiation and relationship management', 'change management and organizational leadership', 'novel market entry and competitive strategy', 'cross-cultural communication and team leadership', 'ethical decision-making and corporate governance', 'entrepreneurship and startup execution', 'crisis management'], ARRAY['AI Project Manager', 'AI Strategy Consultant/AI Transformation Consultant', 'Data-Driven Strategist', 'Automation Consultant', 'Business Operations Analyst — AI and Automation', 'Digital Marketing Manager', 'Customer Experience Designer', 'ESG/Sustainability Analyst'], ARRAY['AI tool literacy (ChatGPT/Copilot/Gemini for business workflows)', 'data analytics (Google Analytics/Power BI/Tableau)', 'project management with AI tools (Asana AI/Monday.com AI)', 'prompt engineering for business use cases', 'change management and digital transformation', 'specialization (digital marketing/supply chain analytics/fintech)'], 'Business Administration remains broadly employable, but generic BA graduates without specialization or AI skill overlay face commoditization. Business graduates who bridge AI and human strategy are most in demand.', 'AI-related management job growth in North America will increase by over 30% within five years, primarily in roles overseeing AI integration and automation strategies (DeWinter Group 2025)', 'DeWinter Group 2025', '85% of employers plan to prioritize upskilling as their primary workforce strategy for 2025-2030.', 'World Economic Forum Future of Jobs Report 2025', 'DLSU (John Gokongwei School of Business); Ateneo SOB; AIM (Asian Institute of Management); UP Diliman College of Business Administration; UST College of Commerce', 'Philippine BPO and shared services sector employs large numbers of BA graduates. AI will automate the routine BPO work, but business development, client management, and strategic roles remain human.', 'Business Administration is safe if you specialize. Generic BA graduates doing administrative work face automation pressure. But the business leader who can navigate AI tools, lead digital transformation, and build client relationships — that person is more valuable than ever. Pick a specialization and add AI fluency.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-004', 'Economics', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 45, 55, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Routine data collection and cleaning', 'standard econometric regression modeling', 'literature reviews and research synthesis', 'economic forecasting using standard models', 'report generation from existing datasets', 'basic policy impact modeling'], ARRAY['Novel theory construction and economic research', 'policy advice and interpretation in politically complex environments', 'behavioral economics and human decision-making analysis', 'regulatory testimony and expert witness roles', 'interpreting structural breaks and anomalies in data', 'communicating economic insights to non-technical audiences'], ARRAY['Economic Automation Consultant', 'AI Economic Modeler', 'Data Economist/Behavioral Data Scientist', 'Technology Policy Economist', 'Climate/ESG Economist', 'Labor Market Economist — AI Impact', 'Development Economist (World Bank/ADB/PH government contexts)'], ARRAY['Python and R for econometric modeling', 'machine learning basics for economic prediction models', 'data visualization (Tableau/Power BI)', 'natural language processing for policy text analysis', 'causal inference and experimental design (A/B testing/RCTs)', 'AI policy and regulation literacy', 'specialization: development/fintech/environmental economics'], 'Economists who master AI tools become significantly more productive and valuable. Demand for economists who can interpret, validate, and communicate AI-generated economic outputs is rising — particularly in NEDA, BSP, DBM, ADB, and World Bank.', 'AI is expected to create approximately $13 trillion in additional global economic activity by 2030 — economists are needed to model, track, and manage this transition (McKinsey Global Institute 2024)', 'McKinsey Global Institute 2024', 'Economists are modeling AI as a productivity multiplier for existing workflows, but the real disruption comes from AI enabling entirely new operational architectures.', 'University of Bristol Working Paper DP25788 2025', 'UP School of Economics (UPSE — consistently the top economics program in PH); DLSU (School of Economics); Ateneo Economics Department; AIM (for applied economics)', 'Philippines has growing demand for economists in NEDA, BSP, PSA, DOF, DBM, and multilateral agencies like ADB (based in Mandaluyong).', 'Economics is transforming rather than declining. AI runs the standard regressions and compiles the data faster than you — but the economist who can design the right question, choose the right model, interpret structural breaks, and advise policymakers is irreplaceable. Add Python, causal inference, and policy specialization.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-009', 'Law', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'Bar Examinations', 17, 44, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Legal document review (due diligence/discovery)', 'contract drafting/markup/comparison', 'legal research and case law synthesis', 'deposition summarization with thematic analysis', 'standard legal correspondence and routine motions', 'compliance monitoring and regulatory tracking', 'immigration paperwork and standard court filings', '60-70% of first-year associate workload'], ARRAY['Trial strategy/courtroom advocacy/oral argument', 'complex negotiations and deal structuring', 'client counseling (especially in distress — divorce/criminal defense/estate disputes)', 'judicial decision-making (cannot be automated — legal/constitutional/ethical barriers)', 'novel legal theory', 'ethics and professional accountability', 'cross-border multi-jurisdictional strategy'], ARRAY['Legal AI Specialist/AI Associate', 'Legal Technology Consultant', 'Legal Prompt Engineer', 'AI Ethics Lawyer (AI liability/regulatory compliance)', 'Data Privacy/Cybersecurity Lawyer', 'Legal Operations Manager', 'Compliance Technology Officer'], ARRAY['Legal AI tools (Harvey AI/Casetext CoCounsel/Westlaw Precision/LexisNexis AI)', 'contract lifecycle management platforms', 'data privacy law (GDPR/Philippine Data Privacy Act)', 'technology transactions and IP in the AI era', 'legal project management', 'mandatory AI literacy'], 'Junior associates doing document review face near-term displacement, but the overall legal profession is expanding. NALP reported 93.4% of 2024 US law graduates employed within 10 months — a record high.', 'Lawyers using AI review analysis close cases 40% faster, enabling bigger caseloads without hiring extra staff (Harvey AI 2025); Goldman Sachs (2023): Generative AI could automate 44% of legal tasks', 'Harvey AI 2025/Goldman Sachs 2023', 'The associates who thrive are those who learn to direct and supervise AI agents, verify their outputs, and focus on judgment-intensive work.', 'Harvey AI Blog 2025', 'UP College of Law (consistently produces Bar topnotchers); Ateneo Law School; DLSU College of Law; San Beda School of Law; UST Faculty of Civil Law', 'Philippines has a large legal sector with growing areas: data privacy law (NPC enforcement), corporate/mergers, labor disputes (AI-related workforce issues), and IP law for tech companies.', 'Law is transforming, not dying. AI now reviews thousands of documents and drafts contracts automatically — but the lawyer who can walk into a courtroom, advise a client facing crisis, and navigate complex regulations is irreplaceable. Learn the AI tools early, specialize in high-value practice areas, and you will command premium rates.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-003', 'Criminology', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'Criminologist Board Exam', 30, 40, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Crime data pattern analysis (hot-spot identification)', 'facial recognition and suspect identification', 'automated forensic evidence processing (DNA database matching/fingerprint matching)', 'predictive policing models (controversial)', 'CCTV video analysis and incident flagging', 'risk assessment scoring tools', 'report writing via AI drafting'], ARRAY['Arrest/detention/use of force decisions (legally and ethically non-delegable)', 'community policing/victim support/restorative justice', 'criminal investigation requiring human judgment and informant management', 'ethical oversight of AI surveillance tools', 'court testimony and expert witness roles', 'rehabilitation and corrections work', 'cybercrime investigation', 'crisis negotiation'], ARRAY['Crime Data Analyst/AI Crime Analyst', 'Predictive Policing Specialist', 'AI Ethics Officer — Law Enforcement', 'Cybercrime Investigator/Digital Forensics Examiner', 'AI Surveillance Auditor', 'Intelligence Analyst with GIS/data science skills', 'Criminal Justice Technology Consultant'], ARRAY['GIS mapping for crime hot-spot analysis', 'data science basics (Python/R/SPSS for crime statistics)', 'digital forensics tools (Cellebrite/Autopsy/Magnet AXIOM)', 'cybersecurity fundamentals', 'AI ethics and civil liberties law', 'OSINT (open-source intelligence) techniques', 'intelligence analysis certification'], 'Criminology is entering a data-intensive phase. 67% of law enforcement agencies are integrating AI analytics by 2025. Jurisdictions using AI have seen 12% workforce growth in data analysis and crime prevention roles.', '90% of law enforcement professionals support AI adoption; one AI model predicted crime a week in advance with 90% accuracy (Actuate AI/Police1 Survey 2025)', 'Actuate AI/Police1 Survey 2025', 'AI can detect patterns in crime data that humans would take months to find — but the officer who builds trust with the community and the investigator who reads between the lines cannot be replaced.', 'US Department of Justice/Council on Criminal Justice December 2024', 'Philippine National Police Academy (PNPA); PNP Training Service; NBI Academy; Criminology programs at FEU, PUP, CEU, and Lyceum', 'Philippines has a large criminology graduate population. PNP, NBI, BJMP, BFP, Bureau of Immigration, and private security are the main employers. Cybercrime (BSP-regulated fraud, NBI cybercrime division) is a fast-growing specialty.', 'Criminology is safe in its core — law enforcement, investigations, and corrections require human judgment and accountability that AI cannot replace. But the data analysis side is growing fast. Criminologists who add digital forensics and AI crime analysis tools to their skillset are highly employable in PNP, NBI, and cybercrime units.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SOC-005', 'Psychology', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'Psychologist/Psychometrician Board Exam', 1, 5, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['Session note-taking and documentation via AI transcription tools', 'symptom tracking and progress monitoring apps', 'scheduling and billing', 'psychoeducation material creation', 'initial psychological assessment scoring', 'AI chatbots for mental health triage and crisis line support (supplementary only)'], ARRAY['Diagnosis of mental health conditions (no FDA-approved AI diagnostic tool as of 2025)', 'crisis intervention and suicide risk assessment', 'complex trauma therapy (EMDR/somatic work)', 'therapeutic relationship building (#1 predictor of therapy outcomes)', 'forensic psychological evaluation', 'neuropsychological testing and interpretation', 'child and adolescent assessment'], ARRAY['AI-Assisted Therapy Supervisor', 'Mental Health Technology Consultant', 'Digital Mental Health Product Designer', 'Telepsychology Specialist', 'Workplace Mental Health Officer (corporate wellness)', 'Neuropsychology/Assessment Specialist', 'Research Psychologist — AI and Human Behavior'], ARRAY['Evidence-based therapy modalities (CBT/DBT/ACT/EMDR)', 'telepsychology and digital health platforms', 'understanding AI mental health tools (to supervise and critique them)', 'neuropsychological assessment', 'industrial-organizational psychology (high corporate demand)', 'trauma-informed care', 'Filipino language/cultural competency'], 'Psychology is among the most AI-resilient professions. Philippines alone has only approximately 11000 licensed psychologists/psychometricians for 110M+ people — massive unmet demand.', 'Mental health counselors have only 0.48% automation probability — one of the lowest of 702 occupations studied (Frey and Osborne Oxford 2013; verified 2025 per WillRobotsTakeMyJob.com)', 'Frey and Osborne/Oxford University 2013; verified 2025', 'As of 2025, there is not an AI tool approved by the FDA to diagnose mental health conditions. AI chatbots cannot manage crisis situations and are not appropriate for moderate-to-severe conditions.', 'Psychology.org/Frontiers in Psychiatry 2025', 'UP Diliman (Department of Psychology — #1 in PH); Ateneo (School of Social Sciences — Psychology); DLSU (Psychology); UST (Psychology); Miriam College', 'Philippines has a massive and growing mental health crisis. The Mental Health Act of 2018 (RA 11036) mandates mental health services in all public hospitals and schools. Only approximately 11000 licensed practitioners for 110M people means extraordinary unmet demand.', 'Psychology is one of the safest careers you can choose. The therapeutic relationship — the trust, the empathy, the clinical judgment built over years of training — is exactly what AI cannot replicate. The Philippines has a severe shortage of mental health professionals. Your career prospects are excellent and your work matters deeply.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SOC-002', 'Guidance and Counseling', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'Guidance Counselor Board Exam', 0, 3, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['Student records management and data entry', 'scheduling appointments', 'college application tracking systems', 'initial career interest inventory scoring', 'generating psychoeducation materials', 'routine email responses and parent communications', 'learning analytics dashboards identifying at-risk students'], ARRAY['Active listening and empathic presence in individual counseling', 'crisis intervention (student suicidality/abuse disclosures — legally mandated human response)', 'family mediation and parent conferences', 'trauma-sensitive response and mandatory reporting decisions', 'IEP development and advocacy', 'cultural and religious sensitivity in student support', 'building trust with at-risk youth'], ARRAY['School Mental Health Coordinator', 'College Counselor + AI Tools Specialist', 'Career Counselor — Tech Sector', 'Student Success Data Analyst', 'Digital Wellness Educator', 'Remote/Online Counselor'], ARRAY['Data literacy (reading and acting on student learning analytics dashboards)', 'familiarity with AI career exploration tools (LinkedIn AI/O*NET/CareerExplorer)', 'mental health first aid and crisis intervention certification', 'trauma-informed counseling approaches', 'college admissions landscape including AI career impacts', 'group counseling and community-based interventions'], 'Guidance and counseling is among the most secure fields due to the relational, contextual, and ethically sensitive nature of the work. Growing awareness of student mental health (post-pandemic) is increasing demand for school counselors across Southeast Asia.', 'Mental health counselors face only 0.5% automation probability, as they require social intelligence and adaptive judgment (Research.com 2026 citing Frey and Osborne methodology)', 'Research.com/Frey and Osborne 2026', 'While automation may reduce demand for routine administrative tasks, it does not eliminate the need for human-centered functions like counseling and advocacy.', 'CASCW/University of Minnesota 2025', 'PNU (Philippine Normal University — premier teacher/counseling education); UP College of Education; Miriam College; UST; Xavier University', 'DepEd mandates a counselor in every school but most schools do not have one — meaning demand far exceeds supply. This creates enormous structural employment demand that no AI can fill.', 'Guidance Counseling is one of the most secure careers available. DepEd mandates a counselor in every school but most schools do not have one — meaning demand far exceeds supply. The crisis intervention, the abuse disclosures, the college counseling conversations — these require a human being, not an app.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SOC-006', 'Social Work', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'Social Worker Board Exam', 10, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Case notes and documentation via AI scribing tools (already used by 21% of social workers)', 'risk assessment data aggregation', 'predictive analytics for child welfare interventions (highly controversial)', 'resource referral matching', 'service eligibility screening and administrative intake'], ARRAY['Home visits and direct observation of family environments', 'mandatory reporting decisions (legally non-delegable)', 'child removal and placement decisions (require human professional judgment)', 'trauma-informed relationship building with clients', 'court testimony and case advocacy', 'cultural humility and community trust-building', 'crisis intervention', 'supervision of less experienced social workers', 'policy advocacy'], ARRAY['Social Work Technologist', 'Community Data Analyst', 'Digital Inclusion Specialist', 'AI Ethics Reviewer — Child Welfare', 'Remote/Telehealth Social Worker', 'Clinical Social Worker (highest-level licensure — most AI-resilient)', 'Policy Analyst with AI tools'], ARRAY['AI documentation tools (to reduce admin burden and increase direct practice time)', 'data analysis basics (for program evaluation and grant writing)', 'critical understanding of AI bias in welfare systems (essential for ethical practice)', 'telehealth/virtual case management', 'evidence-based practice models', 'trauma-informed care certification'], 'Social work is structurally AI-resilient because its core value — human dignity, relationship, advocacy — cannot be encoded. In the Philippines, where social protection infrastructure is underdeveloped, demand for social workers in DSWD, LGUs, and NGOs will significantly outpace supply.', 'Only 21% of social workers currently use AI tools daily (Community Care Poll October 2024); core direct practice functions are considered largely irreplaceable by the ILO and OECD', 'Community Care/ILO/OECD 2024-2025', 'Generative AI tools can help social workers with administrative tasks, allowing more time for direct practice services.', 'CASCW/University of Minnesota 2025', 'UP Diliman (Department of Social Work); UST (Social Work program); La Salle College Antipolo; National College of Social Work and Community Development', 'Philippines has DSWD as a major employer with 4Ps, Sustainable Livelihood Program, and other social protection programs all needing social workers. LGU-based social workers are mandated but severely understaffed.', 'Social Work is a secure career because it is fundamentally about human relationships and community advocacy — things AI cannot do. The Philippines has a massive unmet need for social workers in government, NGOs, and communities. AI will help you with the paperwork so you can focus on the families who need you.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('IT-005', 'Library and Information Science', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'Librarian Board Exam', 30, 50, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Routine cataloguing and metadata tagging via AI-assisted cataloguing tools', 'basic reference queries and FAQ responses via chatbots', 'collection deduplication and weeding', 'interlibrary loan administration', 'literature search assistance (AI tools like Consensus/Elicit/Semantic Scholar)', 'standard bibliographic formatting', 'library circulation desk functions'], ARRAY['Deep research consultation (specialized collections/archival research guidance)', 'collection development requiring subject expertise and community knowledge', 'information literacy instruction and teaching (critical thinking education)', 'archival preservation and special collections management', 'community engagement and programming', 'curating for cultural heritage', 'digital equity work for underserved communities'], ARRAY['AI Librarian (emerging tenure-track role — San Jose State University pioneered this)', 'Research Data Manager', 'Digital Preservation Specialist', 'Knowledge Management Officer (corporate/government libraries)', 'Information Architect', 'Metadata Specialist — AI Training Data', 'Competitive Intelligence Analyst', 'Information Literacy Educator/AI Literacy Educator'], ARRAY['AI-assisted cataloguing tools (Ex Libris/OCLC AI features)', 'research data management (RDM) and data curation', 'digital preservation standards (PREMIS/Dublin Core/OAIS)', 'information literacy instruction methods', 'Python basics for data wrangling and metadata work', 'AI literacy education (teaching others to evaluate AI-generated information)', 'intellectual property and open access policy'], 'Traditional circulation and basic reference roles will shrink, but the information explosion driven by AI increases the need for skilled information professionals who can evaluate, curate, and teach critical use of information.', 'Over 45% of library science jobs are expected to integrate AI technologies by 2028; new AI Librarian tenure-track positions are emerging at institutions like San Jose State University (Research.com 2026)', 'Research.com/San Jose State University iSchool 2026', 'Automation of routine cataloguing is freeing professionals to focus on strategic information services and user engagement.', 'Liblime/American Library Association 2025', 'UP Diliman (School of Library and Information Studies — SLIS, PH only graduate-level library school); PLM; UP Manila; Silliman University', 'Philippine National Library, DLSU-Manila Rizal Library, and university special libraries are the main employers. AI literacy education is a growing specialty — teaching students to critically evaluate AI-generated information is one of the most needed skills in PH schools today.', 'Library Science is transforming into information science. The person who can navigate, curate, and critically evaluate information in an ocean of AI-generated content is more valuable than ever — not less. The AI Librarian is becoming a real job. Add digital preservation, research data management, and AI literacy instruction to your toolkit.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('TEA-003', 'Education', 'Education/Sciences/Others', TRUE, 'Licensure Exam for Teachers (LET)', 25, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Generating lesson plans and worksheets', 'automated grading of multiple-choice and short-answer tests', 'personalized drill exercises (Khan Academy AI tutors)', 'administrative paperwork', 'basic student progress tracking', 'producing differentiated learning materials', 'quiz and assessment item banks'], ARRAY['Emotional support and mentorship', 'classroom management and discipline', 'motivating disengaged students', 'reading social dynamics in a classroom', 'moral and values formation', 'community-embedded teaching in under-resourced rural Philippine schools', 'parent relations', 'guiding children through trauma/grief/home instability', 'co-curricular coaching'], ARRAY['AI-Assisted Learning Designer', 'Educational Technology Integrator', 'Learning Analytics Specialist (DepEd or private schools)', 'AI Curriculum Reviewer for CHED/DepEd compliance', 'Online Tutoring Content Creator pairing AI with live coaching'], ARRAY['AI tool literacy (ChatGPT/Khan Academy AI/Google Gemini for Education)', 'learning analytics and data interpretation', 'differentiated instruction using AI outputs', 'social-emotional learning (SEL) facilitation', 'content creation using AI (prompting and fact-checking)', 'digital citizenship education delivery'], 'Teaching remains one of the most human-irreplaceable professions globally. WEF 2025 projects education professionals among the top 10 growing roles by 2030 driven by demographics. Teachers who integrate AI as a co-teacher outperform those who do not.', 'UNESCO 2025 report on AI in Education explicitly states AI should augment — not replace — teachers, emphasizing human agency as central to the 2030 education agenda. WEF 2025: Education professionals are a net-growing job category through 2030.', 'UNESCO/WEF Future of Jobs 2025', 'AI will be the best tutor... but the relationship between a student and teacher will remain important.', 'Bill Gates, GatesNotes 2023', 'PNU (Philippine Normal University — premier teacher education institution); UP College of Education; Cebu Normal University; Mindanao State University; Western Mindanao State University; all SUCs with Teacher Education programs', 'DepEd is the largest employer in the Philippines with approximately 900000 public school teachers. The student-to-teacher ratio of 1:45+ means demand far exceeds supply. AI tools will enhance Philippine teachers productivity especially for the massive administrative burden.', 'Teaching is one of the safest careers in the Philippines. DepEd is the largest employer in the country and demand far exceeds supply. AI can generate worksheets and grade multiple choice tests, but the teacher who shows up for a student who is struggling at home — who motivates, mentors, and values-forms — that is irreplaceable.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ARCH-001', 'Architecture', 'Education/Sciences/Others', TRUE, 'Architect Licensure Exam (ALE)', 35, 45, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Generative design ideation (Midjourney/DALL-E/Adobe Firefly generating concept visuals in seconds)', 'parametric 3D modeling optimization', 'structural load calculations', 'energy efficiency simulations', 'BIM documentation', 'code compliance checking', 'rendering and visualization', 'repetitive drafting tasks in CAD'], ARRAY['Site visits and contextual design judgment', 'client relationship management', 'community and cultural sensitivity in design (critical in Philippine vernacular and heritage architecture)', 'navigating local government permitting (LGUs)', 'translating client needs into spatial experiences', 'construction supervision', 'designing for climate resilience and disaster risk reduction — highly relevant in the Philippines'], ARRAY['AI Design Prompt Specialist for architectural firms', 'Computational Design Engineer', 'Sustainable Design Consultant using AI simulation tools', 'BIM + AI Integration Specialist', 'Heritage Architecture Documentation using AI photogrammetry', 'Disaster-Resilient Design Consultant'], ARRAY['Proficiency in AI design tools (Midjourney for concept ideation/Autodesk Forma/Spacemaker AI for urban planning/TestFit)', 'computational design thinking', 'parametric modeling (Grasshopper/Rhino)', 'climate-adaptive and passive design principles', 'LEED/BERDE (Philippines green building) certification', 'BIM Level 2/3 proficiency'], 'Architecture is transforming more than disappearing. The licensed architect remains legally required for projects. The competitive edge shifts to those who use AI tools to produce better, faster, more sustainable designs.', 'Goldman Sachs (2023) estimates architecture-related tasks (especially design iteration and documentation) are 30-50% automatable; McKinsey: AI could automate 40-60% of architecture-adjacent knowledge work activities by mid-2030s', 'Goldman Sachs/McKinsey 2023', 'AI can generate a thousand design options overnight. The architect''s job is to know which one is right for the community, the culture, the climate, and the client.', 'American Institute of Architects (AIA) 2024', 'UP College of Architecture (UPCFA — top architecture school in PH); Mapua University (Architecture); DLSU; UST; University of San Carlos Cebu', 'Philippines is highly vulnerable to typhoons, earthquakes, and flooding — disaster-resilient and climate-adaptive architecture design is a national priority. Heritage conservation (Intramuros/Vigan) creates a unique local specialty.', 'Architecture is transforming with AI tools handling the repetitive drafting and basic design variations. But you still design the building that fits the culture, survives the typhoon, and meets the LGU requirements. Learn BIM, generative design tools, and sustainable design — and your career is strong.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SCI-005', 'Biology / Life Sciences', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 30, 40, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Literature review and research synthesis', 'DNA/gene sequence analysis (AlphaFold for protein structure prediction)', 'microscope image analysis and cell counting', 'ecological data pattern recognition', 'drug screening in silico', 'biodiversity data processing from sensor networks', 'taxonomic identification via image recognition'], ARRAY['Field research and specimen collection (especially in Philippine biodiversity hotspots)', 'experimental hypothesis design', 'ethical oversight of research involving organisms or ecosystems', 'science communication and policy advocacy', 'novel discovery and cross-disciplinary synthesis', 'teaching and mentorship', 'regulatory and biosafety compliance'], ARRAY['Bioinformatician', 'Computational Biologist', 'AI-Assisted Drug Discovery Researcher', 'Conservation Data Scientist', 'Genomics Data Analyst', 'Environmental Monitoring Tech Specialist', 'Lab Automation Technician'], ARRAY['Bioinformatics fundamentals (Python/R for biological data)', 'familiarity with AlphaFold/BLAST/QIIME for microbiome analysis', 'statistical modeling for ecological data', 'science communication and grant writing using AI', 'CRISPR/gene editing awareness', 'environmental DNA (eDNA) sampling techniques'], 'Life sciences is among the highest-growth sectors for AI investment. The Philippines, as a megadiverse nation, has significant opportunity in biodiversity informatics, marine biology research, and pharmaceutical plant-based discovery.', 'DeepMind AlphaFold has predicted structures for over 200 million proteins — a task that would have taken humans centuries — yet biological research, experimentation, and fieldwork is more valuable than ever (DeepMind/Nature 2023)', 'DeepMind/Nature 2023', 'AI accelerates discovery, but the curiosity, the hypothesis, the fieldwork in unexplored Philippine ecosystems — that remains irreducibly human.', 'McKinsey Global Institute 2023', 'UP Diliman (IMBB; IBS; Marine Science Institute); UPLB (Institute of Biological Sciences); Ateneo (Biology/Life Sciences); Silliman University (marine biology)', 'Philippines is the center of marine biodiversity (Coral Triangle). Philippine Genome Center (PGC) at UP Diliman is building genomics capacity. Pharmaceutical industry and biotech startups create emerging employment.', 'Biology is a growing field, not a shrinking one. AI tools like AlphaFold are transforming research speed — but the fieldwork in Philippine coral reefs, the experimental design, and the scientific judgment still need you. Add bioinformatics to your training and you bridge biology with the most in-demand tech skills.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SCI-007', 'Chemistry', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 35, 45, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Reaction pathway prediction (AI retrosynthesis tools like IBM RXN)', 'spectral data analysis (NMR/IR interpretation)', 'literature mining for synthesis routes', 'quality control testing in manufacturing', 'materials property prediction', 'formulation optimization in pharma and cosmetics', 'lab documentation and reporting'], ARRAY['Experimental design and novel synthesis', 'safety handling of hazardous materials (requires physical presence and judgment)', 'scale-up and process engineering', 'regulatory compliance (FDA/BFAD Philippines)', 'teaching practical lab skills', 'applied research in local contexts (Philippine natural products chemistry — coconut/narra/guava-based compounds)', 'troubleshooting failed experiments'], ARRAY['Computational Chemist', 'AI-Assisted Materials Scientist', 'Green Chemistry Specialist', 'Pharmaceutical Data Analyst', 'Chemistry AI Trainer (teaching AI models on molecular data)', 'Natural Products Researcher using AI screening tools'], ARRAY['Computational chemistry fundamentals (Gaussian/ORCA or open-source tools)', 'Python for chemical data (RDKit)', 'AI-assisted literature review', 'green chemistry and sustainability principles', 'regulatory affairs knowledge (FDA/BFAD)', 'science communication'], 'Chemistry will see significant augmentation by AI — particularly in pharmaceutical discovery, materials science, and environmental chemistry. Chemists who master computational tools will be highly competitive.', 'IBM RXN for Chemistry AI can predict the outcome of chemical reactions with approximately 90% accuracy; McKinsey identifies R&D as one of the four major business functions where AI delivers the most value, particularly in life sciences and chemical industries', 'IBM/McKinsey 2023-2024', 'AI is not replacing chemists — it is giving them superpowers.', 'Martin Brudermüller, BASF CEO 2024', 'UP Diliman (Institute of Chemistry — top chemistry program in PH); DLSU (Chemistry); UST (Chemistry); Ateneo (Chemistry/Bio-chemistry); Mindanao State University', 'Philippine pharmaceutical industry, food processing, and petrochemical sector employ chemistry graduates. Natural products chemistry (plant-based medicines using Philippine biodiversity) is a unique local specialty.', 'Chemistry is transforming with AI doing the routine spectra analysis and reaction predictions. But you still design novel experiments, handle hazardous materials safely, navigate Philippine BFAD regulations, and develop natural products chemistry that draws on our unique biodiversity.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SCI-002', 'Physics', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 25, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Data analysis from particle detectors/telescopes/sensors', 'numerical simulations (fluid dynamics/quantum systems)', 'literature review and equation solving assistance', 'materials property modeling', 'signal processing and noise filtering', 'pattern recognition in experimental data'], ARRAY['Theoretical physics and novel conceptual frameworks', 'experimental design and instrumentation', 'physics teaching and science communication', 'applied research for Philippine engineering needs (earthquake engineering/climate modeling/nuclear technology for energy)', 'interdisciplinary research leadership'], ARRAY['AI Simulation Engineer', 'Quantum Computing Researcher', 'Data Physicist in tech firms', 'Computational Physicist for renewable energy modeling', 'Space Technology Analyst (Philippine Space Agency)', 'AI Hardware Specialist'], ARRAY['Scientific Python (NumPy/SciPy/TensorFlow for physics)', 'machine learning for physical systems', 'quantum computing literacy (IBM Q/Qiskit)', 'computational fluid dynamics', 'data visualization', 'science policy and communication'], 'Physics is the foundational discipline for the next wave of technology — quantum computing, fusion energy, advanced materials, AI chips. Applied physicists are increasingly in demand at tech companies and national research institutions.', 'Oxford Frey-Osborne (2013) classified physicists at only 7% probability of computerization — among the lowest of all 702 occupations; WEF 2025: technological R&D professionals among top fastest-growing roles by net increase', 'Oxford Frey-Osborne/WEF 2025', 'The most important contribution physicists can make is to ensure AI is built on sound mathematical and physical principles.', 'IEEE Address summary 2024', 'UP Diliman (National Institute of Physics — NIP, #1 in PH); DLSU (Physics); Ateneo (Physics); MSU-IIT (Applied Physics)', 'Philippine Space Agency (PhilSA) created in 2019 creates new opportunities for applied physicists. DOST-ASTI, PNRI, and PAGASA all employ physicists. Renewable energy modeling is a growing application.', 'Physics is one of the safest and most future-proof degrees you can take. AI runs on mathematics and physics — the people who deeply understand both will be the ones building and auditing the AI systems that run the world. A physics degree opens doors to data science, AI research, quantum computing, and space technology.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SCI-001', 'Mathematics and Statistics', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 40, 55, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Routine statistical computation', 'data cleaning and preprocessing', 'standard regression and machine learning model building', 'generating reports and data summaries', 'solving textbook-level problems', 'basic actuarial table calculations', 'survey data tabulation'], ARRAY['Novel mathematical proof and theory development', 'model selection and assumption validation', 'statistical consulting and expert judgment', 'communicating results to non-technical stakeholders', 'research design', 'ethical oversight of algorithmic models', 'teaching mathematical reasoning and problem-solving'], ARRAY['Data Scientist', 'Machine Learning Engineer', 'Quantitative Analyst (Quant) in finance', 'Biostatistician in pharma/health research', 'AI Ethics Auditor', 'Actuarial Data Scientist', 'Operations Research Analyst', 'Government Statistician (PSA expansion)'], ARRAY['Python and R for data science', 'SQL and database management', 'machine learning and deep learning (Scikit-learn/PyTorch/TensorFlow)', 'statistical communication and data storytelling', 'probability theory for AI/ML', 'causal inference methods', 'certifications: Google Data Analytics/IBM Data Science Professional Certificate'], 'Mathematics and statistics graduates are among the most AI-proof at the skills level — because AI itself runs on math. Demand shifts from manual calculation toward modeling, interpretation, and AI oversight. Data science is the #1 fastest-growing role in WEF 2025.', 'WEF Future of Jobs Report 2025: Big data specialists and AI/machine learning specialists are the #1 and #3 fastest-growing roles by percentage through 2030', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025', 'Mathematical/statistical occupations are among those most likely to be complemented — not displaced — by AI, with technology amplifying rather than replacing statistical expertise.', 'Goldman Sachs Research 2023', 'UP Diliman (Institute of Mathematics; Institute of Statistics — top programs in PH); DLSU (Mathematics/Statistics); Ateneo (Mathematics); MSU-IIT; UP Visayas', 'Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA), Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP), NEDA, and DOST-SEAMO are major employers of statisticians. Data science skills from Math/Statistics graduates are in high demand in Philippine banks, telcos, and tech companies.', 'Math and Statistics graduates are well-positioned in the AI era because AI runs on mathematics. The question shifts from doing the calculation to knowing which calculation to run, validating the model assumptions, and communicating results to decision-makers. Add Python and data science skills and you are among the most employable graduates in the country.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SCI-009', 'Geology', 'Education/Sciences/Others', TRUE, 'Geologist Board Exam', 30, 40, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Seismic data interpretation (AI processing thousands of seismic traces)', 'satellite/remote sensing imagery analysis for geological mapping', 'mineral prospectivity mapping', 'well log analysis', 'terrain modeling from LiDAR data', 'routine laboratory mineral identification via spectroscopy AI', 'climate and volcanic hazard pattern recognition'], ARRAY['Field mapping and rock sampling', 'interpreting geological context requiring local knowledge', 'communicating disaster risk to LGUs and communities', 'regulatory compliance for mining permits', 'geotechnical assessment for construction', 'volcanic eruption and earthquake response (PHIVOLCS-critical role)', 'cross-disciplinary environmental impact assessment'], ARRAY['Geospatial Data Analyst', 'Remote Sensing Specialist for geological survey', 'AI-Assisted Mineral Exploration Analyst', 'Climate Change Geoscientist', 'Geohazard Risk Modeler', 'Carbon Capture Site Assessment Geologist'], ARRAY['GIS and remote sensing (ArcGIS/QGIS/Google Earth Engine)', 'Python for geospatial analysis', 'machine learning for seismic interpretation', 'knowledge of Philippine geology (Ring of Fire/PHIVOLCS standards)', 'environmental geology and hazard assessment', 'drone operation for geological survey'], 'Geology has strong Philippine relevance — the country sits on the Ring of Fire with 24 active volcanoes and frequent seismic activity. PHIVOLCS, MGB, and NAMRIA all represent steady public sector demand.', 'Oxford Frey-Osborne (2013) estimated geoscientists at only 22% probability of computerization; the Philippines MGB consistently employs geologists for hazard mapping — a role that requires fieldwork and cannot be fully automated', 'Oxford Frey-Osborne/MGB Philippines 2025', 'The geologist who can read AI-processed satellite data and then verify it with a hammer in the field — that combination is irreplaceable.', 'PHIVOLCS/MGB Philippines 2024', 'UP Diliman (National Institute of Geological Sciences — NIGS, top geology program in PH); MSU-IIT; Mapua; Mindanao State University; UP Baguio', 'Philippines sits on the Pacific Ring of Fire with 24 active volcanoes, frequent major earthquakes, and active mining in Mindanao and Visayas. MGB, PHIVOLCS, and NAMRIA are primary public sector employers.', 'Geology is essential for the Philippines given our place on the Ring of Fire. Your fieldwork — mapping hazards, assessing mining sites, responding to volcanic activity — cannot be replaced by AI. The technology makes you faster and more accurate. Add GIS and remote sensing skills and your career in MGB, PHIVOLCS, or mining becomes extremely strong.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-013', 'Agriculture', 'Education/Sciences/Others', TRUE, 'Agriculturist Board Exam', 30, 40, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Crop disease identification via smartphone AI (PlantVillage/Plantix apps)', 'drone-based aerial crop monitoring', 'precision irrigation control using soil sensors and AI', 'weather pattern analysis for planting schedules', 'supply chain logistics optimization', 'livestock behavior monitoring', 'yield prediction models', 'pest and weed detection via computer vision'], ARRAY['Farm management decision-making in resource-constrained Philippine smallholder settings', 'community agriculture extension work', 'farmer training and technology adoption facilitation', 'soil health judgment in the field', 'indigenous seed variety preservation', 'agricultural policy and food security advocacy', 'agro-ecological systems design'], ARRAY['Precision Agriculture Technician', 'Agricultural Data Analyst', 'Drone Operator for Crop Monitoring', 'Smart Irrigation Systems Specialist', 'AgTech Startup Founder', 'Agricultural AI Extension Officer (DA/ATI-type roles with tech focus)', 'Food Systems Sustainability Consultant'], ARRAY['Drone operation and aerial data analysis', 'GIS for agriculture (ArcGIS/QGIS)', 'data-driven farm management (Agrivi/FarmLogs/HARA for SE Asia)', 'IoT sensors for soil/climate monitoring', 'basic data analysis (Excel to Python)', 'agri-finance and value chain management', 'knowledge of Philippine DA programs and SAAD'], 'WEF 2025 projects farmworkers and agricultural roles as the single largest job growth category globally — 34 million new jobs added by 2030. Philippine food security agenda and climate-smart agriculture push create strong domestic demand.', 'WEF Future of Jobs Report 2025: Agricultural workers top the list of the 15 largest net-growing jobs globally by 2030 — an estimated 34 million additional roles', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025', 'Precision agriculture AI tools could increase crop yields 15-20% while reducing water use by 30% — creating high demand for agricultural professionals who can operate these systems.', 'McKinsey Global Institute 2023', 'UPLB (University of the Philippines Los Baños — #1 in PH for agriculture); Visayas State University; BSU Benguet State University; Central Luzon State University; Bukidnon State University', 'Philippines is highly vulnerable to climate change with agriculture as the most-affected sector. DA SAAD program and the emerging AgTech startup scene create new pathways for tech-integrated agriculturists.', 'Agriculture is one of the safest careers you can choose because feeding people is non-negotiable and the Philippines cannot afford to get it wrong. AI helps with crop monitoring and precision irrigation — but the extension work, the farmer training, the adaptation to Philippine conditions — those need you. WEF says this is the #1 job growth category by 2030.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-011', 'Fisheries Technology', 'Education/Sciences/Others', TRUE, 'Fisheries Technologist Board Exam', 25, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Fish stock assessment modeling from sonar/acoustic data', 'water quality monitoring via IoT sensors', 'AI-powered fish identification from underwater cameras', 'automated feeding systems in aquaculture', 'satellite-based illegal fishing detection (Global Fishing Watch)', 'supply chain traceability using blockchain/AI', 'market price prediction models'], ARRAY['Coastal community engagement and livelihood programs', 'artisanal fishing management and traditional knowledge preservation', 'vessel operations and seamanship', 'field-based environmental impact assessment', 'regulatory enforcement (BFAR)', 'coral reef and mangrove rehabilitation fieldwork', 'disaster response and post-typhoon assessment of coastal fisheries'], ARRAY['Aquaculture Technology Specialist', 'Fisheries Data Analyst', 'Maritime IoT Systems Operator', 'Sustainable Fisheries Certification Consultant', 'Coastal GIS Analyst', 'Blue Economy Researcher'], ARRAY['IoT and sensor systems for aquaculture', 'GIS for coastal resource management', 'knowledge of BFAR regulations and Philippine Fisheries Code', 'data literacy (fish stock modeling/water quality analytics)', 'sustainable aquaculture certification', 'climate adaptation planning for coastal communities'], 'Philippines — an archipelago with 36289 km of coastline — has enormous blue economy potential. AI tools like Global Fishing Watch are being adopted by BFAR and international NGOs. Tech-enabled fisheries management is a critical career growth area.', 'Global Fishing Watch (supported by Google) uses AI to monitor 60000+ vessels globally in near real-time; Philippines is one of the world''s top fishing nations and a major deployment context (Global Fishing Watch/FAO 2024)', 'Global Fishing Watch/FAO 2024', '600 million livelihoods globally depend on fisheries — tech-enabled fisheries management is a critical career growth area for the next decade.', 'FAO State of World Fisheries Report 2022', 'UPLB (College of Fisheries and Ocean Sciences); DNSC (Don Mariano Marcos State University); Mindanao State University (fisheries); UP Visayas (Miag-ao campus); Western Philippines University', 'Philippines is one of the world''s top fishing nations and a signatory to the Port State Measures Agreement against illegal fishing. BFAR and international conservation organizations (WWF/WCS/IUCN Philippines) are growing employers.', 'Fisheries Technology has strong job security because the Philippines depends on fisheries for food security and the livelihoods of millions of coastal Filipinos. AI is making monitoring and management better — and that requires trained fisheries professionals to operate and interpret the technology. Your local knowledge of Philippine waters and communities is your advantage.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('MAR-001', 'Marine Transportation', 'Education/Sciences/Others', TRUE, 'Marine Deck Officer Board Exam', 30, 45, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Autopilot and route optimization (already standard — AI-assisted collision avoidance)', 'weather routing AI', 'predictive maintenance for ship engines', 'cargo load optimization algorithms', 'port logistics and berthing scheduling', 'administrative documentation (customs/manifests)', 'fuel consumption optimization via AI'], ARRAY['Final navigational decisions in complex sea conditions/emergencies/piracy situations', 'crew management and safety leadership', 'port authority negotiations', 'STCW compliance requiring human certification', 'crisis response (fire/flooding/man overboard)', 'diplomatic and communication roles with port officials', 'cargo inspection and damage assessment'], ARRAY['Maritime Cyber Security Officer', 'Autonomous Vessel Operations Monitor', 'Smart Ship Systems Technician', 'Fleet Data Analyst for shipping companies', 'Maritime AI Safety Auditor', 'E-Navigation Specialist'], ARRAY['E-navigation and ECDIS (Electronic Chart Display) proficiency', 'GMDSS (Global Maritime Distress and Safety System) advanced', 'cyber security awareness (IMO 2021 cyber risk mandate)', 'maritime data analytics', 'autonomous ship monitoring systems', 'English proficiency for international routing'], 'The IMO is developing a regulatory framework for Maritime Autonomous Surface Ships (MASS). Full autonomy remains 10-20 years away for commercial shipping; however, the role of officers shifts from helmsmen to systems monitors and safety overseers.', 'Philippines supplies approximately 25% of the world''s merchant marine workforce — about 400000 active seafarers globally (MARINA/International Transport Workers Federation data 2025)', 'MARINA/ITF 2025', 'The sea remains unpredictable. An AI can plot the optimal course, but it cannot negotiate with a port captain in Lagos or make a life-or-death decision in a typhoon.', 'IMO International Maritime Organization MASS Regulatory Framework 2025', 'Philippine Merchant Marine Academy (PMMA — Cavite, state-run); John B. Lacson Maritime University (Iloilo); Cebu Maritime University; San Pedro College of Business Administration (Maritime)', 'Philippines supplies approximately 25% of global seafarers — one of the country''s most important exports. The shift to e-navigation and autonomous vessel monitoring requires upgraded training. Filipino seafarers earn premium global wages.', 'Marine Transportation is a strong career for the Philippines — we supply 1 in 4 of the world''s seafarers. AI is handling navigation assistance and predictive maintenance, but your STCW certification, seamanship, and human judgment in emergencies remain essential. Add e-navigation and cyber security training for the autonomous ship era.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ENG-003', 'Aviation', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 25, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Autopilot systems (handle approximately 90% of flight time already)', 'AI-assisted air traffic management', 'predictive aircraft maintenance (GE Predix/Airbus Skywise)', 'flight path optimization for fuel efficiency', 'structural design simulation (FEA automated by AI)', 'cabin crew scheduling optimization', 'incident/accident pattern recognition'], ARRAY['Takeoff/landing/emergency response (FAA/CAAP regulations require licensed pilots)', 'in-flight anomaly judgment', 'crew resource management (CRM)', 'airline customer interaction', 'regulatory compliance and airworthiness sign-off', 'aeronautical research and novel aircraft design', 'air traffic control final authority', 'aircraft accident investigation'], ARRAY['Aviation AI Safety Analyst', 'Unmanned Aerial Systems (UAS/Drone) Operator and Regulator', 'Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) Engineer', 'Advanced Air Mobility (AAM/eVTOL) Pilot and Engineer', 'Aviation Cyber Security Specialist', 'MRO Data Analyst'], ARRAY['Human Factors and CRM (Crew Resource Management) excellence', 'drone/UAS operation and CAAP regulations', 'aviation data analytics', 'AI systems monitoring and override protocols', 'sustainable aviation engineering principles', 'ATPL (Airline Transport Pilot License)', 'digital avionics proficiency'], 'Aviation industry growing rapidly post-pandemic — IATA projects air passenger numbers to double by 2040. Autopilot advances moving toward single-pilot operations, but full automation is constrained by regulation and public acceptance.', 'FAA and CAAP regulations mandate two licensed pilots on commercial flights; any rule change is at least a decade away. Airbus tested DragonFly autonomous emergency landing system in 2023 — but human pilots remain legally required (Airbus/FAA/CAAP 2023)', 'Airbus/FAA/CAAP 2023-2025', 'Aviation requires pilots who understand both the physical aerodynamics and the AI systems managing the aircraft. The safest pilot in 2030 is the one who knows when to override the machine.', 'IATA Safety Report/ICAO 2024', 'PATTS College of Aeronautics (Paranaque); OMNI Aviation Corporation (Clark); Philippine Airlines Aviation School; CAAP-accredited flying schools', 'Philippine aviation sector is growing significantly — new airports (Bulacan/Cavite/Clark expansion), and Cebu Pacific/Philippine Airlines fleet expansion are driving pilot demand. CAAP requires Filipino pilots to meet international standards. Drone regulation is being formalized — a growing domestic specialty.', 'Aviation is a safe and growing career. The FAA and CAAP require licensed human pilots on every commercial flight — that is not changing anytime soon. AI makes flying safer by handling routine tasks, but your judgment in emergencies and your certification remain legally required. The growing Philippine aviation sector means strong local demand.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('BUS-003', 'Tourism and Hospitality Management', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 40, 55, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['AI chatbot concierge services (24/7 booking assistance/FAQ response)', 'automated check-in/check-out (kiosks/facial recognition)', 'revenue management and dynamic pricing algorithms', 'travel itinerary personalization (Booking.com AI/Expedia AI)', 'routine email response', 'loyalty program management', 'multilingual translation services', 'social media monitoring and review responses'], ARRAY['High-touch luxury hospitality and personalized guest experiences', 'culturally nuanced service (especially in Philippine bayanihan hospitality culture)', 'handling guest complaints and emotional situations', 'destination storytelling and local cultural interpretation', 'event planning and execution', 'front-of-house leadership', 'community-based tourism facilitation', 'crisis management (typhoons/health emergencies)'], ARRAY['Tourism Experience Designer (creating AI-personalized itineraries)', 'Hospitality Technology Manager', 'Destination Marketing Specialist using AI analytics', 'Sustainable Tourism Consultant', 'Agritourism and Eco-Tourism Developer', 'Digital Concierge Content Curator', 'Tourism Data Analyst'], ARRAY['CRM systems (Salesforce/HubSpot) and property management systems (Opera PMS)', 'revenue management software (IDeaS/Duetto)', 'digital marketing and SEO for tourism', 'social media management with AI tools', 'data analytics for tourism demand forecasting', 'sustainable tourism certification', 'foreign language proficiency'], 'Tourism is both disrupted and growing — WTTC projects the sector to contribute $15.5 trillion to global GDP by 2033. Philippines DOT targets 12 million international arrivals by 2028. AI automates the transactional layer, elevating human-layer hospitality.', 'World Travel and Tourism Council (WTTC) projects the sector to contribute $15.5 trillion to global GDP by 2033; Philippines DOT targets 12 million international arrivals by 2028', 'WTTC/DOT Philippines 2024', 'McKinsey: Customer operations AI tools are projected to handle 60-70% of routine tourism inquiries by 2030 — but the human layer in luxury and cultural tourism keeps growing.', 'McKinsey Global Institute 2023', 'UP College of Home Economics (Tourism Management); DLSU (Tourism and Hospitality Management); Lyceum of the Philippines University (pioneered HRM education in PH); De La Salle College of Saint Benilde; Enderun Colleges (international focus)', 'Philippines is one of Southeast Asia''s top tourism destinations. DOT targets ambitious arrivals growth. Community-based and eco-tourism is a growing niche. Cruise industry expansion (Manila Bay/Cagayan de Oro) creates new hospitality roles.', 'Tourism and Hospitality careers are safe at the high end and under pressure at the low end. AI will handle booking chatbots and automated check-ins — but the experience designer who crafts a Palawan eco-tour, the event planner who runs a 500-person conference, and the front-office manager who diffuses a guest crisis — those roles need you.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-002', 'Mass Communication and Journalism', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 40, 60, 2, 'At Risk', '#EF4444', ARRAY['Automated financial and sports news writing (AP has used AI since 2014', 'Bloomberg uses Cyborg for earnings reports)', 'social media post drafting', 'SEO article generation', 'basic press release summarization', 'video transcript editing', 'headline optimization A/B testing', 'data visualization for journalism', 'audio editing and podcast transcription'], ARRAY['Investigative journalism (source cultivation/whistleblower handling/legal risk navigation)', 'breaking news reporting in the field', 'political reporting and accountability journalism', 'cultural criticism and opinion writing', 'documentary storytelling', 'live broadcasting performance', 'editorial judgment on what is newsworthy', 'ethical decision-making', 'community journalism and local news (critical in Philippine regional media)'], ARRAY['AI Content Editor/Fact-Checker', 'Audience Analytics Specialist', 'Multimedia Journalist (text + video + data)', 'Computational Journalist using data journalism tools', 'AI Ethics Reporter', 'Content Strategy Director', 'Podcast Producer', 'Misinformation Researcher and Digital Literacy Advocate'], ARRAY['Data journalism (tools: Flourish/Datawrapper/Python for journalism)', 'AI literacy and prompt-based content production', 'video production and editing (Adobe Premiere/CapCut/DaVinci Resolve)', 'digital verification and fact-checking (First Draft/InVID/Google Reverse Image)', 'social media algorithm literacy', 'SEO and audience analytics', 'multimedia storytelling', 'investigative research methods'], 'Traditional journalism jobs are under severe pressure — newsrooms globally reduced headcount 15-30% between 2020-2024, with AI cited as a contributing factor. However, demand for trusted, human-authored content is rising as AI misinformation proliferates.', 'The Associated Press generates approximately 3700 financial news stories per quarter using AI (Automated Insights/Wordsmith since 2014); Reuters uses Lynx Insight AI to assist journalists in newsroom analysis (AP/Reuters 2024)', 'AP/Reuters 2024', 'The value of journalism is not in writing words — it is in asking the questions an algorithm cannot think to ask.', 'Reuters Institute Digital News Report 2024', 'UP College of Mass Communication (UPCMC — premier journalism school in PH); DLSU (AB Communications/Journalism); Ateneo (AB Communications); UST College of Fine Arts, Sciences, and Technology (Journalism); NUJP-affiliated schools', 'Philippine media landscape includes major networks (ABS-CBN/GMA/CNN Philippines), online news platforms (Rappler/Inquirer/PCIJ), and a large regional media ecosystem. Fact-checking in the PH context (one of world''s most targeted countries for misinformation) is a critical growing specialty.', 'Mass Communication and Journalism are honestly at risk for commodity content work — AI already writes financial news and sports scores. But investigative journalism, accountability reporting, and documentary storytelling are irreplaceable. The Philippines has one of the world''s most active misinformation environments — human journalists who can verify facts and hold power accountable are more important than ever.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('ARCH-003', 'Fine Arts and Multimedia Arts', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 40, 65, 2, 'At Risk', '#EF4444', ARRAY['AI image generation (Midjourney/DALL-E 3/Stable Diffusion/Adobe Firefly) replacing stock illustration and concept art', 'video generation (OpenAI Sora/Runway ML) replacing basic motion graphic production', 'copywriting and advertising copy drafts', 'logo and branding variations', 'social media content batch production', '3D modeling from text prompts', 'music generation for background ads', 'A/B testing of ad creative variations'], ARRAY['Conceptual strategy and brand narrative development', 'art direction and creative vision', 'campaign concepts requiring cultural insight (Filipino pop culture/regional humor/bayanihan values)', 'client relationship management and pitching', 'ethical and legal oversight of AI-generated content', 'fine art as cultural expression and social commentary', 'exhibition curation', 'performance and installation art', 'photography with authentic human perspective'], ARRAY['AI Art Director (prompting/curating/refining AI outputs at scale)', 'Creative AI Trainer (building brand-specific AI models)', 'UX/UI Designer specializing in AI-generated interfaces', 'Brand Authenticity Consultant', 'Digital Rights and AI Art Ethics Specialist', 'Generative AI Content Strategist', 'Metaverse and Immersive Experience Designer', 'NFT/Digital Asset Curator'], ARRAY['AI creative tools mastery (Midjourney/Adobe Firefly/Stable Diffusion/Runway ML)', 'brand strategy and creative direction beyond execution', 'Adobe Creative Suite + AI integration', 'motion design (After Effects)', 'UX/UI design (Figma)', 'digital advertising platforms (Meta Ads/Google Ads AI tools/TikTok Ads Manager)', 'copyright law as applied to AI-generated work'], 'The entry-level execution layer (junior designers producing ad variations/social media graphics/stock illustrations) is being rapidly commoditized by AI. The strategic, conceptual, and brand-building layer is growing. WEF ranks creative thinking as #2 rising human skill through 2030.', 'Adobe Firefly AI generated over 1 billion images in its first three months (Adobe 2023); Goldman Sachs estimates 25-50% of marketing and content workloads automatable by AI; WEF 2025: Creative thinking ranks #2 among rising human skills through 2030', 'Adobe/Goldman Sachs/WEF 2023-2025', 'Creative thinking is ranked as the second most important rising human skill through 2030 — AI can generate, but it cannot innovate with cultural insight.', 'World Economic Forum Future of Jobs 2025', 'UP College of Fine Arts (UPCFA); CSB (College of Saint Benilde — strong creative/design focus); DLSU (Multimedia Arts); Ateneo (Fine Arts/Visual Communications); iACADEMY; AMA Computer University (Digital Arts)', 'Philippine creative industry is vibrant — advertising agencies (J. Walter Thompson/BBDO/Publicis), game development (Synergy88/Anino), animation (Toei Animation Philippines), and the growing OPM/content creator economy. The Filipino visual identity and cultural insight remain powerful differentiators.', 'Fine Arts and Multimedia Arts face the most honest disruption of any creative field. AI can already generate images, videos, and ad copy in seconds. The question is: can you do what AI cannot — build the brand strategy, understand the Filipino market, direct the creative vision, and protect your client''s identity from generic AI output? Master the AI tools and position yourself as the creative director, not the executor.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('OTH-001', 'Political Science', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 35, 50, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Routine legislative research and document summarization', 'basic policy brief drafting', 'news monitoring and political event tracking', 'constituent data analysis', 'standard government report generation'], ARRAY['Policy analysis and strategic interpretation in complex political environments', 'advocacy and stakeholder negotiation', 'diplomatic relations and foreign service work', 'legislative debate and floor work', 'political campaign strategy', 'community organizing and grassroots mobilization', 'human rights advocacy'], ARRAY['AI Policy Analyst (governments and NGOs hiring for AI governance roles)', 'Political Data Scientist', 'Legislative AI Advisor', 'Digital Democracy Researcher', 'Disinformation Analyst', 'Foreign Service Officer (AI literacy-enhanced)'], ARRAY['Data analytics and political polling (R/Python)', 'AI policy and governance literacy (essential — this is a booming niche)', 'GIS for electoral mapping', 'social media listening tools for political sentiment', 'policy writing and legislative drafting', 'public speaking and debate', 'international relations frameworks'], 'Political Science is transforming into a data-intensive field. The AI governance and regulation space is one of the fastest-growing policy areas globally — Political Science graduates who understand both policy and AI are in extraordinary demand in government, think tanks, and multilateral organizations.', 'AI governance and regulation is now one of the top 5 fastest-growing areas of government hiring globally; Political Science + AI policy expertise is among the most in-demand combinations in OECD government agencies (OECD AI Policy Observatory, 2025)', 'OECD AI Policy Observatory 2025', 'The most important decisions about AI — who controls it, who benefits, who is harmed — are political decisions, not technical ones.', 'Marietje Schaake, former European Parliament AI advisor, 2024', 'UP Diliman (Department of Political Science — consistently the top PolSci program in PH); Ateneo (Political Science); DLSU (Political Science); UST; De La Salle Araneta', 'Philippines has a large government sector including Congress, DILG, DFA, NEDA, CHED, and hundreds of LGUs employing Political Science graduates. The Commission on Elections (COMELEC), PCGG, and various constitutional commissions are major employers. AI regulation is an emerging policy area with the DICT leading the national AI roadmap.', 'Political Science is transforming into one of the most relevant degrees for the AI era — not because you build AI, but because you govern it. Every government agency needs people who can write AI policy, analyze political data, and advocate for ethical technology. The politicians and diplomats who understand AI will shape the next decade.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('BUS-003-dup-47', 'Hotel and Restaurant Management', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 40, 55, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Reservation management via AI booking systems', 'automated check-in/check-out kiosks', 'menu optimization and food cost analysis via AI tools', 'inventory management and supply ordering automation', 'basic customer complaint routing', 'staff scheduling optimization algorithms'], ARRAY['Hands-on food preparation and culinary artistry', 'personalized luxury guest service and relationship management', 'kitchen brigade leadership and food safety oversight', 'wine pairing and sommelier expertise', 'live event and banquet coordination', 'training and managing diverse service teams', 'handling VIP guest experiences requiring emotional intelligence'], ARRAY['Food and Beverage Technology Manager', 'AI-Augmented Revenue Manager', 'Restaurant Experience Designer', 'Smart Kitchen Operations Specialist', 'Culinary Content Creator (food media/social media)', 'Sustainable Food Systems Manager', 'Corporate Dining and Catering Manager'], ARRAY['Property Management Systems (Opera PMS/Oracle Hospitality)', 'revenue management tools (IDeaS/EzRMS)', 'digital menu platforms (TouchBistro/Toast AI)', 'food safety management systems (HACCP digital tools)', 'social media marketing for food and hospitality', 'culinary arts and food costing', 'ServSafe/TESDA food safety certifications'], 'HRM is both disrupted (front-desk automation, digital ordering) and growing (experiential dining, wellness hospitality, food tourism). The Philippine hospitality sector is one of the fastest-growing employment sectors, with DOT targeting significant tourism revenue increases.', 'The Philippines hospitality sector contributed approximately 12.7% to GDP in 2024 and is growing — DOT targets 12 million international arrivals by 2028, creating sustained HRM employment demand (DOT Philippines/WTTC 2024)', 'DOT Philippines/WTTC 2024', 'In hospitality, AI handles the transaction — but the memory, the warmth, the story of the meal belongs to the human who served it.', 'Cornell School of Hotel Administration, Hospitality Technology Summit 2024', 'DLSU (Tourism and Hospitality Management); De La Salle College of Saint Benilde (HRM — strong industry connections); Enderun Colleges; Lyceum of the Philippines University (pioneered HRM in PH); UP College of Home Economics', 'Philippines has one of Asia''s strongest hospitality workforces with a reputation for warmth and service excellence. The OFW hospitality sector (cruise ships, luxury hotels in Middle East/US/Singapore) creates premium employment. Filipino chefs and hotel managers command global respect.', 'HRM is safe at the level that matters most — the art of hospitality, the skill of cooking, the management of people and experiences. AI handles the booking and the inventory. You provide the service excellence that makes guests come back. Specialize in culinary arts, event management, or luxury hospitality for the best career trajectory.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('SCI-008', 'Environmental Science', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 25, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Satellite imagery analysis for environmental monitoring', 'automated air and water quality sensor data processing', 'climate model runs and scenario simulations', 'environmental compliance report generation from standard templates', 'species distribution modeling from existing databases'], ARRAY['Field environmental assessment and ground-truthing', 'environmental impact assessment (EIA) requiring on-site judgment', 'community consultation and indigenous peoples engagement (FPIC process)', 'regulatory negotiation with DENR and LGUs', 'climate adaptation planning requiring local knowledge', 'disaster risk reduction and environmental emergency response', 'novel ecosystem research in Philippine biodiversity hotspots'], ARRAY['Climate Data Scientist', 'Environmental AI Analyst', 'Carbon Market Specialist (carbon credits/REDD+)', 'Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) Consultant', 'Sustainability Manager (ESG roles in corporations growing rapidly)', 'Climate Resilience Planner', 'Circular Economy Specialist'], ARRAY['GIS and remote sensing (ArcGIS/Google Earth Engine/QGIS)', 'Python for environmental data analysis', 'climate modeling tools (CMIP6/IPCC datasets)', 'LiDAR and drone operation for environmental surveys', 'ESG reporting frameworks (GRI/TCFD/ISSB)', 'environmental law and DENR regulations', 'community engagement and participatory research methods'], 'Environmental Science is one of the highest-growth career fields globally. The climate crisis, ESG reporting requirements, and corporate sustainability mandates are creating massive demand for environmental professionals. WEF 2025 lists Environmental Engineers among the top 15 fastest-growing jobs.', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025: Environmental and Renewable Energy Engineers are among the top 15 fastest-growing roles globally; ESG reporting is now mandatory for listed companies in 60+ countries, creating massive new demand for environmental professionals', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025 / GRI/ISSB 2025', 'Climate change is the defining challenge of this century. Environmental scientists are not a nice-to-have — they are essential infrastructure.', 'UN Environment Programme (UNEP) / IPCC Working Group III, 2025', 'UP Diliman (Institute of Environmental Science and Meteorology — IESM; Marine Science Institute); UPLB (Institute of Environmental Science); Ateneo (Environmental Science COD); Miriam College (strong environmental science program with active research partnerships)', 'Philippines is one of the world''s most climate-vulnerable countries — ranked among the top 10 annually by the Global Climate Risk Index. DENR, DOST-PAGASA, PCAARRD, and the Climate Change Commission all employ Environmental Science graduates. The rapidly growing ESG compliance market creates corporate demand.', 'Environmental Science is one of the safest and most future-proof degrees you can take. The climate crisis means the world desperately needs people who can measure, analyze, and solve environmental problems. AI gives you better tools for satellite monitoring and climate modeling — but the fieldwork, the community engagement, and the policy advocacy are still yours.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-sociology', 'Sociology', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 35, 45, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Routine survey data collection and tabulation', 'basic statistical analysis of social data', 'literature review and research synthesis', 'generating standard demographic reports', 'social media data scraping and basic sentiment analysis'], ARRAY['Ethnographic fieldwork and in-depth interviews requiring human presence and trust-building', 'interpretive analysis of cultural and social phenomena', 'social theory development and application', 'community-based participatory research', 'policy advocacy and social impact evaluation', 'teaching and mentoring', 'cross-cultural analysis requiring contextual understanding'], ARRAY['Computational Sociologist (combining sociology theory with big data analysis)', 'Social Data Analyst', 'Community Research Specialist', 'UX Researcher (sociology background is excellent preparation)', 'Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Analyst', 'Social Impact Evaluator', 'AI Ethics Researcher (sociological lens on algorithmic bias)'], ARRAY['Quantitative social research methods (R/SPSS/Python for social science)', 'qualitative research tools (NVivo/Atlas.ti)', 'survey design and mixed-methods research', 'social network analysis', 'data visualization for non-technical audiences', 'policy writing and advocacy communication', 'community organizing and facilitation'], 'Sociology is transforming — the field increasingly overlaps with data science (computational social science), UX research, and AI ethics. Sociologists who add quantitative skills are highly employable in tech companies, government, and NGOs.', 'Computational social science is one of the fastest-growing academic fields globally, with sociology graduates who add data skills commanding 40-60% salary premiums over pure social science peers (American Sociological Association 2025)', 'American Sociological Association 2025', 'Sociologists are among the most important people in the AI era — they are the ones who will tell us whether the algorithm is reproducing inequality.', 'danah boyd, Data & Society Research Institute, 2024', 'UP Diliman (Department of Sociology — top sociology program in PH; strong research tradition); Ateneo (Sociology/Behavioral Sciences); DLSU; UST; UP Visayas', 'Philippines has active sociological research in areas like migration (OFW communities), urban poverty, regional development, and agrarian reform. DSWD, NEDA, and multilateral organizations (ILO, UN agencies) employ sociologists. The growing tech sector needs social scientists to evaluate AI fairness and community impact.', 'Sociology is transforming into one of the most relevant fields for understanding and critiquing the AI revolution. The sociologist who can analyze algorithmic bias, study how technology reshapes communities, and advise companies on social impact is in growing demand. Add data analysis skills and you bridge two worlds that need each other.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-anthropology', 'Anthropology', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 25, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Basic literature reviews and research synthesis', 'transcription of recorded interviews and field notes', 'initial categorization and coding of qualitative data', 'museum catalog digitization and standard archival documentation'], ARRAY['Ethnographic fieldwork requiring long-term community immersion and trust', 'interpretation of cultural practices and symbolic meaning', 'indigenous peoples consultation and cultural heritage protection', 'archaeological excavation and site interpretation', 'forensic anthropology (human remains identification for legal cases)', 'applied anthropology in development projects and disaster response'], ARRAY['UX Researcher / Design Anthropologist (tech companies)', 'Cultural Intelligence Consultant (for corporations entering new markets)', 'AI Ethics Advisor (anthropological lens on cultural bias in algorithms)', 'Forensic Anthropologist', 'Heritage and Cultural Resource Manager', 'Development Anthropologist (NGOs/multilateral agencies)', 'Applied Anthropologist in health and medical research'], ARRAY['Ethnographic research methods and participant observation', 'qualitative data analysis (NVivo/Atlas.ti)', 'cultural competency and cross-cultural communication', 'digital anthropology and online community research', 'human-computer interaction (HCI) research methods', 'applied research and evidence-based program design', 'language learning (multiple Philippine languages/dialects is a major advantage)'], 'Anthropology is a niche but resilient field. The rise of tech companies expanding into diverse cultural markets has created significant demand for anthropologists in UX research, international expansion, and AI ethics — roles that were rare 10 years ago.', 'Tech companies including Google, Microsoft, Intel, and IBM employ anthropologists specifically for UX research, cultural product design, and AI ethics — a trend that has grown 300% since 2018 (EPIC — Ethnographic Praxis in Industry Conference, 2025)', 'EPIC (Ethnographic Praxis in Industry Conference) 2025', 'The most human thing about AI is that humans built it — and anthropologists are the ones who will tell us what that means.', 'Michael M.J. Fischer, MIT Program in Science, Technology, and Society, 2024', 'UP Diliman (Department of Anthropology — the primary anthropology program in PH; Archaeological Studies Program); Ateneo (Anthropology/Sociology); San Carlos University Cebu (strong Visayan ethnography tradition)', 'Philippines has extraordinary anthropological richness — over 110 ethnolinguistic groups, active indigenous peoples communities (IP rights under RA 8371 IPRA), and rich archaeological heritage (Tabon Man, Callao Man). NCIP, NHC, NHCP, and National Museum employ anthropologists. International NGOs working with IPs hire applied anthropologists.', 'Anthropology is a surprisingly robust career in the AI era. Tech companies now hire anthropologists to help them understand the people their products affect — and the Philippines'' extraordinary cultural diversity gives Filipino anthropology graduates a unique perspective. Add UX research skills and you can work in tech, development, or cultural heritage.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-development-communication', 'Development Communication', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 30, 45, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Generating standard IEC (Information-Education-Communication) materials', 'basic social media content drafting for NGO campaigns', 'routine progress reports and donor updates', 'data visualization for standard program indicators', 'translation of technical research into plain language summaries'], ARRAY['Community needs assessment and participatory communication planning', 'facilitating community dialogue and consensus-building processes', 'designing communication campaigns that account for local culture and context (critical in Philippines with 100+ languages/dialects)', 'radio and community media production for remote areas', 'implementing SBCC (Social and Behavior Change Communication) for health programs', 'documenting indigenous knowledge and community stories'], ARRAY['Development Communication Specialist (NGOs/UN agencies/USAID/ADB)', 'Social and Behavior Change Communication (SBCC) Designer', 'Community Media Producer', 'Digital Inclusion Officer (bridging technology gaps in rural areas)', 'AI Literacy Educator for underserved communities', 'Impact Communication Strategist', 'Participatory Research Facilitator'], ARRAY['Community radio production and multimedia storytelling', 'participatory research methods (FGD/KII/PRA)', 'SBCC frameworks (behavior change communication for health/environment programs)', 'digital media literacy and community media tools', 'project management for development programs (PMD Pro)', 'grant writing and donor reporting', 'language skills in Filipino regional languages'], 'Development Communication is a niche but stable field with consistent demand from international development organizations. The Philippines, as a recipient of significant ODA (Official Development Assistance) from USAID, EU, ADB, World Bank, and bilateral donors, creates steady employment for DevCom graduates.', 'UPLB is the only university in Southeast Asia offering a BS Development Communication degree — its graduates are employed across 50+ countries in UN agencies, international NGOs, and government development programs (UPLB College of Development Communication, 2025)', 'UPLB College of Development Communication 2025', 'Technology does not reach communities — communication does. Development communicators ensure that the benefits of innovation actually arrive at the people who need them most.', 'UNICEF Communication for Development (C4D) Framework, 2024', 'UPLB (College of Development Communication — the only dedicated DevCom college in Southeast Asia, uniquely positioned); Miriam College; UP Open University (development communication distance learning programs)', 'Philippines is one of the world''s major recipients of international development assistance. USAID, EU, ADB, World Bank, UN agencies (UNICEF, FAO, WHO, WFP), and hundreds of NGOs employ Development Communication specialists. The DENR, DOH, and DA also employ DevCom graduates for extension and public communication programs.', 'Development Communication is a niche career with a loyal employer base. UPLB''s DevCom program has alumni working in over 50 countries for the UN, USAID, and international NGOs. AI will automate the template-writing — but the community dialogue, the participatory communication planning, and the cultural translation work that makes development programs actually reach people — that is still yours.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-customs-administration', 'Customs Administration', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', TRUE, 'Customs Broker Licensure Exam', 55, 70, 2, 'At Risk', '#EF4444', ARRAY['Document verification and customs declaration processing (AI now handles 60-70% of routine clearance)', 'tariff classification for standard goods (AI databases do this automatically)', 'risk assessment scoring for cargo inspection (AI profiling systems)', 'invoice verification and duty computation for standard transactions', 'standard compliance report generation'], ARRAY['Complex tariff classification disputes and legal interpretation', 'physical inspection of goods requiring trained judgment (contraband, hazardous materials, misdeclared cargo)', 'trade facilitation negotiations with importers/exporters', 'customs enforcement operations (anti-smuggling, intellectual property violations)', 'post-clearance audit requiring forensic accounting', 'policy interpretation for novel goods and technologies', 'cross-border legal disputes and arbitration'], ARRAY['Trade Compliance Technology Specialist', 'AI Customs Systems Auditor', 'International Trade Compliance Officer', 'Customs Data Analyst', 'Trade Facilitation Consultant', 'E-Commerce Customs Specialist (rapidly growing with cross-border e-commerce boom)'], ARRAY['AI customs clearance platforms (understanding how they work to oversee and audit them)', 'tariff classification systems (HS Code mastery remains essential)', 'trade compliance management software (SAP GTS/Oracle Global Trade Management)', 'international trade law (ASEAN FTAs, WTO/GATT)', 'customs risk management', 'anti-smuggling intelligence methods'], 'Routine customs processing is being automated rapidly — the Bureau of Customs (BOC) is deploying AI-assisted clearance systems. However, complex trade compliance, enforcement, and dispute resolution roles remain firmly human. The e-commerce boom creates new customs challenges that AI cannot fully address.', 'The Bureau of Customs processed over P3 trillion in revenue in 2024; AI-assisted risk selectivity systems now handle an estimated 60-70% of routine clearance automatically, shifting customs brokers toward complex case advisory roles (BOC Philippines Annual Report 2024)', 'Bureau of Customs Philippines Annual Report 2024', 'Customs AI can classify a standard container of electronics. It cannot negotiate with a smuggler, testify in court, or interpret a novel tariff dispute involving goods that did not exist when the law was written.', 'World Customs Organization (WCO) Technology Conference 2024', 'PUP (Polytechnic University of the Philippines — largest Customs Administration program in PH); University of the East (UE); Philippine Christian University; PLM; National College of Business and Arts (NCBA)', 'Philippines has a large customs broker profession. The Bureau of Customs (BOC) is the second-largest revenue-collecting agency after BIR. E-commerce growth (Lazada, Shopee, Temu cross-border imports) is creating significant new customs compliance work that requires human expertise in novel tariff situations.', 'Customs Administration is honest — routine document processing is being automated fast. But the customs broker who handles complex tariff disputes, leads anti-smuggling investigations, and navigates the rapidly changing world of e-commerce customs regulations is still very much needed. Specialize in trade compliance, enforcement, or e-commerce customs to stay ahead.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-office-administration', 'Office Administration', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 65, 80, 2, 'At Risk', '#EF4444', ARRAY['Calendar and schedule management (AI assistants)', 'email drafting and correspondence', 'document preparation and formatting', 'data entry and records management', 'basic bookkeeping and expense reporting', 'meeting coordination and minutes-taking', 'filing and document retrieval', 'receptionist and front-desk functions'], ARRAY['Complex executive support requiring judgment and discretion', 'sensitive stakeholder communication and relationship management', 'project coordination across multiple departments', 'office systems design and workflow improvement', 'training and supervising junior administrative staff', 'crisis and emergency administrative support', 'confidential record management'], ARRAY['AI-Augmented Executive Assistant', 'Office Systems Automation Specialist', 'Administrative Technology Trainer', 'Document Management Specialist', 'Executive Operations Coordinator (senior-level support for C-suite)', 'Virtual Assistant specializing in high-value executive support'], ARRAY['AI office tools proficiency (Microsoft Copilot 365/Google Workspace AI/Notion AI)', 'project management tools (Asana/Monday/ClickUp)', 'advanced Excel and data management', 'business communication and professional writing', 'event planning and coordination', 'records management and information systems', 'executive support skills'], 'Entry-level administrative tasks are among the most exposed to AI automation. However, senior executive support, office systems management, and administrative leadership roles remain valuable. The career path requires moving up and specializing — generic admin roles face the greatest pressure.', 'Administrative assistants and office clerks are listed among the fastest-declining occupations by the WEF Future of Jobs 2025 — with an estimated 11-14 million roles declining globally by 2030 due to AI-driven automation', 'WEF Future of Jobs 2025', 'The administrative assistant who can manage AI tools, run office systems, and support executive decision-making will be indispensable. The one who only types letters will be replaced.', 'Harvard Business Review / Gartner 2025', 'PUP (large Office Administration program); PLM; Pamantasan ng Lungsod ng Maynila; many SUCs and community colleges offer this program', 'This is an honest assessment — Office Administration faces the highest automation risk of any program in this list. The path forward is specialization: AI tool expertise, executive support, project coordination, or using this degree as a stepping stone to business management. Students choosing this course should be aware of the transition requirement.', 'Office Administration is one of the most honest conversations about AI''s impact. Routine admin work — scheduling, filing, data entry, correspondence — is being automated fast. The path forward is clear: become the person who manages and optimizes the AI office tools, or specialize in executive support and complex project coordination where judgment matters. Do not plan to do routine admin work in 2030.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-foreign-languages', 'Foreign Languages', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 30, 50, 3, 'Transforming', '#F59E0B', ARRAY['Basic translation of standard documents (AI translation tools like DeepL/Google Translate handle high-volume routine translation)', 'transcription of recorded foreign-language content', 'simple interpreting for routine business meetings', 'language tutoring for basic vocabulary and grammar (AI language apps like Duolingo replace routine drilling)'], ARRAY['Simultaneous and consecutive interpretation for high-stakes settings (court proceedings, diplomatic meetings, UN sessions — where errors have legal or political consequences)', 'literary and cultural translation requiring nuance and creativity', 'language teaching at advanced levels with cultural context', 'diplomatic and consular work', 'cross-cultural negotiation and business mediation', 'foreign service and international relations', 'certified legal and medical interpretation'], ARRAY['Certified Court Interpreter / Legal Interpreter', 'Language Quality Assurance Specialist (reviewing AI translations for high-stakes content)', 'AI Language Trainer (training multilingual AI models on underrepresented languages)', 'Cultural Consultant for multinational companies', 'Foreign Service Officer', 'Korean/Japanese/Mandarin Business Liaison (in-demand in PH BPO and business sectors)', 'Language Technology Specialist'], ARRAY['Advanced proficiency in target language (C1/C2 CEFR level — this is the non-negotiable floor)', 'cultural competency and area studies knowledge', 'AI translation tool oversight and quality assurance', 'specialized domain knowledge (legal/medical/technical translation is harder to automate)', 'interpretation techniques (simultaneous, consecutive, whisper)', 'certification pathways (court interpreter, DFA exams)'], 'AI translation has fundamentally changed the field — routine, high-volume translation is commoditized. However, the demand for high-quality, culturally nuanced, legally precise, and diplomatically sensitive language work remains strong. Languages like Korean, Japanese, and Mandarin have surging demand in the Philippines specifically.', 'Korean and Japanese language proficiency commands a 30-50% salary premium in the Philippine BPO/shared services sector, driven by demand from Korean and Japanese companies with Philippine operations (IBPAP/JobStreet Philippines 2025); DeepL and similar AI tools are replacing 60-70% of routine document translation volume', 'IBPAP/JobStreet Philippines 2025', 'AI can translate words. Only a human can translate meaning — the cultural context, the unspoken implication, the diplomatic nuance that determines whether a negotiation succeeds or fails.', 'UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) / International Association of Conference Interpreters (AIIC), 2024', 'UP Diliman (Asian Center — Japanese/Korean/Chinese studies; Department of European Languages); Ateneo (foreign language programs); UST (foreign language programs); Centro Escolar University; FEU (East Asia Center for foreign languages)', 'Philippines is a major Asian hub for Korean and Japanese companies, with Korean investments and BPO operations creating sustained demand for Korean-Filipino bilingual professionals. Mandarin speakers are in demand in the growing Chinese-affiliated business sector. The DFA Foreign Service exam is a major career pathway. UN Volunteer programs and ASEAN Secretariat roles employ language specialists.', 'Foreign Languages is transforming, not dying. AI handles routine translation — your value is in the high-stakes, culturally complex, legally precise work that machines still get wrong. Korean, Japanese, and Mandarin speakers have exceptional demand in the Philippine market right now. Pair your language skills with specialization in law, medicine, business, or diplomacy for the strongest career.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-filipino-and-philippine-literature', 'Filipino and Philippine Literature', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 20, 30, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Basic content translation from Filipino to English or vice versa', 'generating standard grammatically correct Filipino text (AI can do this but at lower cultural quality)', 'cataloging and indexing Filipino literary works', 'routine Filipino language teaching drilling exercises'], ARRAY['Creative writing, poetry, and literary fiction in Filipino — expressing authentic Filipino cultural voice', 'literary criticism and cultural analysis requiring deep cultural knowledge', 'Filipino language teaching at advanced levels (grammar, rhetoric, literature)', 'cultural heritage documentation (oral literature, regional languages and dialects)', 'media writing in Filipino (broadcast journalism, film scripts, stage productions)', 'editing and publishing of Filipino-language content'], ARRAY['Filipino Content Writer/Copywriter (Filipino-language digital content is massively underserved by AI)', 'Filipino Media Professional (broadcast/film/theater)', 'Language Educator and Curriculum Developer', 'Cultural Heritage Documentation Specialist', 'Filipino Literary Publisher and Editor', 'AI Filipino Language Trainer (teaching AI models proper Filipino — there is real commercial demand for this)'], ARRAY['Advanced Filipino writing and rhetoric', 'Philippine literary tradition and cultural history', 'regional language competency (Tagalog, Bisaya, Ilokano, Kapampangan — multilingualism is a major advantage)', 'creative writing across genres', 'media production (broadcast scripts, digital content)', 'Filipino grammar and linguistics', 'cultural research methods'], 'Filipino language expertise is AI-resilient precisely because AI models struggle with Filipino — the language is underrepresented in training data, so Filipino-language content quality from AI is poor compared to English. Filipino language professionals who can produce high-quality cultural content have significant advantages in the local media and digital market.', 'Filipino and Philippine regional languages are significantly underrepresented in major AI training datasets — ChatGPT, Gemini, and Claude all produce lower-quality output in Filipino compared to English, creating genuine demand for Filipino language professionals to train and correct AI models (Meta AI Language Report 2024 / AI training industry analysis)', 'Meta AI Language Report 2024', 'The Filipino language carries the history, humor, and soul of a people that no algorithm can replicate. Its literature is the most honest record of who we are.', 'National Artist Virgilio S. Almario, Komisyon sa Wikang Filipino, 2024', 'UP Diliman (Department of Filipino and Philippine Literature — the premier Filipino studies program; Sentro ng Wikang Filipino); PNU (Philippine Normal University — strong Filipino language education program); Ateneo (Filipino Studies); UST (Filipino); MSU-Marawi (Maranao and Mindanaoan languages research)', 'Filipino language professionals are in demand in broadcast media (ABS-CBN, GMA, PTV), film and theater, publishing (Adarna House, Anvil Publishing), government communications (KWF, PCO), and education (DepEd Filipino curriculum). The AI era creates a new niche — Filipino language specialists who can train and quality-check AI models on Filipino text.', 'Filipino is actually one of the more AI-resistant language careers because AI still struggles with authentic Filipino. Your deep knowledge of Filipino culture, literature, and language nuance is something no model trained primarily on English can match. The local media, education, and AI training industries all need you — and your work preserves Filipino cultural identity.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-history', 'History', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 20, 30, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Digitizing and cataloging archival documents', 'basic bibliographic research', 'chronological fact-checking using databases', 'generating standard historical summaries from established sources', 'organizing secondary literature into research bibliographies'], ARRAY['Original archival research and primary source interpretation', 'writing historical narratives that require judgment and contextualization', 'oral history collection and community memory preservation', 'forensic historical analysis for legal and policy purposes', 'museum curation and public history education', 'historical consulting for film, media, and policy', 'critical analysis of AI-generated historical content for accuracy and bias'], ARRAY['Archivist / Digital Preservation Specialist', 'Public Historian and Museum Curator', 'Historical Consultant (film/media/policy)', 'Oral History Researcher', 'Heritage Site Manager', 'AI Content Fact-Checker (historians are increasingly employed to verify AI-generated historical claims)', 'Policy Researcher with Historical Analysis specialization'], ARRAY['Archival research methods and primary source analysis', 'digital humanities tools (Omeka/ArcGIS for historical mapping/Zotero)', 'oral history interviewing and recording techniques', 'public history and museum studies', 'historical writing and narrative', 'policy analysis drawing on historical precedent', 'Filipino history and cultural heritage (essential for local employment)'], 'History is a field where AI augments but rarely replaces — because historical interpretation requires judgment, cultural context, and the synthesis of incomplete and contradictory evidence. The growing misinformation crisis actually increases demand for historians who can verify claims and provide accurate context.', 'The misinformation industry and AI hallucination problem have created new demand for historically trained fact-checkers — major news organizations and tech companies are hiring historians specifically to audit AI-generated historical content (Poynter Institute / Reuters Institute 2025)', 'Poynter Institute / Reuters Institute 2025', 'The historian is the memory of civilization. In an age of synthetic media and algorithmic misinformation, that memory has never been more essential.', 'National Historical Commission of the Philippines (NHCP) Director, 2024', 'UP Diliman (Department of History — top history program in PH; Philippine Studies program); Ateneo (History Department); UST (Department of History); De La Salle University (History); San Carlos University Cebu (strong Visayan history research)', 'Philippines has a rich and contested historical narrative — the National Historical Commission of the Philippines (NHCP), National Archives, National Library, and National Museum employ historians. Academic positions in Philippine universities remain stable. The misinformation landscape in the Philippines (ranked among the world''s most disinformation-affected countries by Reuters Institute) creates new demand for historically trained fact-checkers.', 'History is more relevant than ever in the age of AI misinformation. Your ability to analyze primary sources, question narratives, and provide accurate historical context is exactly what newsrooms, fact-checkers, and institutions need. Philippine history is also one of the most contested and important fields — your work helps the nation understand itself honestly.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-philosophy', 'Philosophy', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 10, 20, 5, 'Very Safe', '#16A34A', ARRAY['Generating introductory explanations of philosophical concepts and theories', 'basic bibliography of philosophical literature', 'summarizing well-known philosophical positions', 'drafting routine ethics committee review templates for standard research protocols'], ARRAY['Original philosophical reasoning and argumentation', 'applied ethics analysis for novel situations (AI ethics, bioethics, tech ethics — all require human philosophical judgment)', 'critical thinking education and Socratic teaching', 'values formation and moral reasoning in educational settings', 'philosophy of mind and consciousness research (directly relevant to AI limitations)', 'religious and cultural ethics consultation', 'legal and policy ethics advisory roles'], ARRAY['AI Ethics Researcher/Officer (one of the fastest-growing roles in tech companies globally)', 'Bioethics Consultant', 'Technology Ethics Advisor (for government, corporations, and multilateral agencies)', 'Philosophy of Mind Researcher (directly relevant to AI consciousness debates)', 'Corporate Ethics Officer', 'Curriculum Designer for Critical Thinking and Ethics', 'Philosophical Counselor / Existential Therapist'], ARRAY['AI ethics frameworks and responsible AI principles (IEEE Ethically Aligned Design', 'EU AI Act', 'Anthropic/OpenAI safety frameworks)', 'critical thinking and argumentation methodology', 'applied ethics (bioethics/technoethics/environmental ethics)', 'logic and formal reasoning (valuable for AI safety research)', 'philosophy of mind and cognitive science (highly relevant to AI consciousness research)', 'communication and teaching of abstract concepts'], 'Philosophy is arguably the most AI-proof and most AI-relevant humanities degree simultaneously. AI ethics is a booming global field, and philosophers are among the most sought-after hires at leading AI companies. The deeper truth: AI cannot do philosophy — consciousness, meaning, and values are precisely where AI falls short.', 'AI ethics roles grew 1,257% in 2024-2025 — the fastest-growing professional category tracked by LinkedIn; philosophy graduates are among the most hired for these roles because of their training in value theory, logic, and critical argumentation (LinkedIn Economic Graph 2025)', 'LinkedIn Economic Graph 2025', 'The most important questions about AI are not technical questions. They are philosophical questions — about consciousness, meaning, value, and what it means to be human. Philosophers are not optional in the AI era. They are essential.', 'Dario Amodei, Anthropic CEO — Machines of Loving Grace, 2024', 'UP Diliman (Department of Philosophy — home of renowned Philippine philosophers; Phronesis journal); Ateneo (Philosophy — strong Jesuit philosophical tradition; Center for Ethics and Religious Studies); UST (Faculty of Philosophy; Thomistic tradition); De La Salle University (Philosophy)', 'Philosophy graduates in the Philippines are employed in education, law (many law school topnotchers have philosophy backgrounds), government ethics offices, religious institutions, and increasingly in the tech sector. The rapidly growing AI ethics field at both the national level (DICT AI ethics working group) and corporate level creates new pathways that did not exist five years ago.', 'Philosophy is secretly one of the best degrees you can take in the AI era. AI companies are literally hiring philosophers to work on ethics, safety, and the meaning of consciousness. Your training in critical thinking, logical argumentation, and value theory is exactly what the world needs to govern AI responsibly. Also — philosophy majors consistently score highest on the LSAT and GRE. Your options are wide open.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-marine-science-marine-biology', 'Marine Science / Marine Biology', 'Education/Sciences/Others', FALSE, NULL, 20, 30, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Automated underwater image analysis and species identification from camera traps', 'satellite oceanography data processing', 'water quality sensor data compilation and basic trend analysis', 'standard scientific literature reviews', 'generating routine oceanographic data reports from existing sensor networks'], ARRAY['SCUBA diving and underwater fieldwork (irreplaceable for reef surveys, specimen collection, and underwater habitat assessment)', 'ship-based oceanographic sampling requiring seamanship', 'coastal community engagement and participatory reef monitoring', 'marine protected area (MPA) monitoring and law enforcement support', 'novel species discovery and ecological research', 'ocean policy advocacy and marine spatial planning', 'coral reef restoration fieldwork'], ARRAY['Marine Data Scientist (combining marine biology with AI-powered satellite oceanography)', 'Underwater Robotics Operator (ROV/AUV systems for deep-sea research)', 'Blue Carbon Specialist (mangroves/seagrass/coral reefs as carbon sinks — fast-growing field)', 'Marine Spatial Planning Analyst', 'Aquaculture Technology Specialist', 'Marine Conservation Program Officer (NGOs/BFAR)', 'Ocean Climate Researcher'], ARRAY['Marine ecology field methods (transect surveys/quadrats/SCUBA certification — PADI/SSI required)', 'eDNA (environmental DNA) sampling and metabarcoding', 'remote sensing for coastal and ocean monitoring (Sentinel/MODIS/SeaWiFS)', 'GIS for marine spatial planning', 'Python for marine data analysis', 'fisheries science and BFAR regulations', 'ocean acidification and climate change impacts on marine ecosystems'], 'Marine Science is a growing field globally and critically important for the Philippines. The blue economy, climate change impacts on marine ecosystems, and international conservation obligations all drive demand for marine scientists. The Philippines, as the center of global marine biodiversity, is a uniquely important location for this work.', 'The Philippines lies at the center of the Coral Triangle — the most biodiverse marine region on Earth — hosting 600+ coral species, 2000+ fish species, and 6 of 7 marine turtle species; marine scientists trained in the Philippines are globally recognized for their expertise (Coral Triangle Initiative / IUCN 2024)', 'Coral Triangle Initiative / IUCN 2024', 'The ocean covers 71% of the Earth''s surface and we have explored less than 20% of it. Marine scientists are not a luxury — they are a necessity for planetary survival.', 'NOAA / Intergovernmental Oceanographic Commission (IOC-UNESCO), 2024', 'UP Diliman (Marine Science Institute — MSI, the premier marine science institution in PH; multiple internationally recognized researchers); UP Visayas (fisheries and marine science); Silliman University (Institute of Environmental and Marine Sciences — strong Dumaguete coral reef research tradition); MSU-IIT (Mindanao marine sciences)', 'Philippines has 36,289 km of coastline — the 5th longest in the world — and sits at the apex of the Coral Triangle. BFAR, DENR-BMB (Biodiversity Management Bureau), PCAMRD, international NGOs (WWF-Philippines, IUCN, WCS, Conservation International), and UN agencies (UNDP, FAO) all employ marine scientists. The growing blue economy and climate change monitoring create new roles.', 'Marine Science is one of the most important and irreplaceable careers for the Philippines. We are the center of global marine biodiversity and one of the most ocean-dependent nations on Earth. AI gives you satellite data and automated species identification — but the reef surveys, the community engagement, and the conservation policy work that protects Philippine waters still need you in the water.', '2026-06-02'),
  ('AI-entrepreneurship', 'Entrepreneurship', 'Business/Law/Social Sciences', FALSE, NULL, 20, 35, 4, 'Safe', '#22C55E', ARRAY['Market research data compilation and basic trend analysis', 'generating standard business plan templates and financial projection spreadsheets', 'routine competitor analysis from publicly available data', 'basic legal document templates (MOA, NDAs for standard use cases)', 'social media content creation for startup marketing'], ARRAY['Vision-setting and strategic direction for a business', 'building and motivating a founding team', 'customer discovery and user research requiring genuine human empathy', 'negotiating with investors, suppliers, and partners', 'managing uncertainty and pivoting based on market feedback', 'creating company culture and values', 'community-building around a brand or mission', 'innovative product ideation from lived experience and customer pain points'], ARRAY['AI Startup Founder (building AI-powered products — the clearest growth path)', 'Social Entrepreneur (AI tools lower barriers to building mission-driven ventures)', 'AgTech/EdTech/HealthTech Entrepreneur (high-impact sectors with Philippine need)', 'Startup Ecosystem Builder (incubators/accelerators/angel networks)', 'Innovation Consultant', 'Business Development Manager (startup-to-enterprise pipeline)', 'Franchise Developer'], ARRAY['Customer discovery and lean startup methodology (Steve Blank/Eric Ries frameworks)', 'financial modeling and unit economics', 'fundraising and investor relations', 'product-market fit validation methods', 'AI tools for startups (no-code/low-code platforms dramatically lowering building costs)', 'digital marketing and growth hacking', 'legal basics for startups (IP, corporate structure, investment terms)', 'pitching and public speaking'], 'Entrepreneurship is the degree most empowered by AI — not threatened by it. AI tools have dramatically lowered the cost and complexity of building a product, reaching customers, and running a business. The constraint is no longer technology; it is vision, execution, and leadership — which are irreducibly human.', 'AI tools have reduced the cost of building an MVP by an estimated 70-80% since 2022 (Y Combinator analysis 2025); no-code/low-code AI platforms mean a non-technical founder can now build and test a product in weeks instead of months — making Entrepreneurship degrees more potent than ever', 'Y Combinator Analysis 2025', 'AI is the greatest equalizer for entrepreneurs. For the first time, a 20-year-old founder with a laptop and a great idea has access to tools that used to require a team of 20.', 'Sam Altman, OpenAI CEO — at Y Combinator Demo Day, 2024', 'AIM (Asian Institute of Management — MBA and entrepreneurship programs; YC alumni network); DLSU (John Gokongwei School of Business — Entrepreneurship); Ateneo (Ateneo Center for Entrepreneurship); UP Diliman (UP Enterprise — startup incubator; ISSI innovation programs); IdeaSpace Foundation (Philippine startup accelerator); QBO Innovation Hub', 'Philippine startup ecosystem is growing — Startup PH Law (RA 11337), IdeaSpace, QBO Innovation Hub, the Ayala/Globe/SM accelerator programs, and the growing tech community (Cebu, Davao, BGC) create a supportive environment. The Philippines has produced several unicorns (Revolution Precrafted, Kumu) and strong regional startups. AI dramatically lowers the barrier to building Philippine-focused products.', 'Entrepreneurship is the degree most accelerated by AI. Every AI tool that lets you build faster, market smarter, and operate leaner makes being an entrepreneur more accessible. Your job is not to be replaced by AI — it is to use AI to build something the world needs. The Philippines needs Filipino founders who understand local problems deeply and can build solutions for them.', '2026-06-02')
